//| v6.5.4 REACTION CONFLICT FIX (see docs/KLJ_V6.5.4_REACTION_CONFLICT_FIX.md):  |
//| 1. "(no liquidity pool in range)" no longer earns 8/12 score points:          |
//|    missing liquidity evidence is 0 (swept 12 > resting 4 > none 0).          |
//| 2. RXN_ApplyOpposition: a CONFIRMED reaction is capped CONFLICTED (REACTION)  |
//|    when the opposing zone rejects price or an opposing BOS/CHoCH/MSS lands    |
//|    after its confirmation bar, and capped STRONG (LIMITED ROOM) when the      |
//|    nearest opposing zone is < InpRXNMinRoomATR (1.0) away with no closed      |
//|    breakout through it. Candidates are collected, guarded, THEN published,    |
//|    so label/alert/record/dashboard all read the same guarded state.           |
//| 3. RXN_LevelEx: HTF and D1 BOTH opposed raises the CONFIRMED gate by          |
//|    InpRXNCountertrendMargin (8). InpRXNOppositionFilter=false = v6.5.3.       |
//| Compiled with MetaEditor: NOT RUN in this environment (F7 is the user's gate).|
//| QuantumSMC_AI_Pro_v6.5.3_SystemReview.mq5                          |
//| v6.5.3 SYSTEM REVIEW - the seven defects reported on the running   |
//| build, each fixed at its cause, none of them deferred:             |
//| D1. ONE prior-period reference. PDH/PDL/PWH/PWL are now resolved   |
//|     by a single closed-bar function (QSMC_PriorClosedPeriod: the   |
//|     last D1/W1 candle fully closed by the chart's decision         |
//|     boundary), with one cache, one availability bar and one        |
//|     reason string, consumed by the S/R cluster, the PMI ledger,    |
//|     the ZRE candidates, the target engine, the top-down row and    |
//|     the scenario context. Two incompatible definitions (position   |
//|     shift-1 vs boundary) could previously publish different daily  |
//|     levels on two charts at once; a disagreement is now logged     |
//|     once, and the level + its availability + its age always come   |
//|     from the same record.                                          |
//| D2. Message consistency. The zone-age dead end ("zone age is       |
//|     unavailable") was caused by level-based candidates carrying no |
//|     birth bar; the S/R cluster, the volume profile and the D1/W1   |
//|     candidates now publish a real birth bar, and the remaining     |
//|     metric-missing texts name the missing METRIC, while FEED       |
//|     health is reported separately (the two no longer contradict    |
//|     each other on one screen). "NO BUY - SUPPORT ACCEPTED" now     |
//|     says the level FAILED (acceptance THROUGH the level).          |
//| D3. Text vs panel width. The docked panel sized and truncated text |
//|     from a hard-coded 6 px per character while drawing with a real |
//|     font; every panel now measures (TextFit/TextWidthPx), sizes    |
//|     its background from the measured text and cuts on a WORD       |
//|     boundary, so a line can no longer end on a fragment or spill   |
//|     outside its own background.                                    |
//| D4. Leftover placeholder words. An indicator-owned text object     |
//|     that exists without text is now impossible: each recalculation |
//|     ends with an ownership sweep that deletes such objects (and    |
//|     logs the name once per session).                               |
//| D5. Rating integrity. Every printed zone strength shows the SAME   |
//|     split (strength = intrinsic + HTF/D1 context) with the same    |
//|     words, and every strength next to a sample count says when the |
//|     sample is insufficient - a weight sum is never presented as a  |
//|     measured statistic.                                            |
//| D6. Chart readability. The sniper tags are short and anchored at   |
//|     their OWN zone instead of one shared column at the newest bar, |
//|     the ZRE projection headline is a short card (full provenance   |
//|     in the tooltip) and the reaction suppression card sits on the  |
//|     last CLOSED bar instead of on the live price.                  |
//| D7. Weighted bias. A documented weighted consensus (D1 50 / H4 30  |
//|     / H1 20, HTF-wins tie-break) is computed once and shown on     |
//|     every panel, so "the timeframes disagree" is never printed     |
//|     without the direction the weights favour and the rule used.    |
//|     The execution gate is UNCHANGED: qualification still requires  |
//|     the full D1/H4/H1 alignment - a conflict stands aside by       |
//|     design, and the panel now says so instead of looking undecided.|
//| No threshold, gate, score weight or historical value was changed.  |
//| Compiled with MetaEditor: NOT RUN in this environment (see         |
//| docs/PART_A_REPAIR_HANDOFF.md - F7 compile is the user's gate).    |
//| v6.5.2 FILE-BY-FILE AUDIT PASS (this build):                       |
//| AUDIT-01 [CRITICAL] Indicators-Access: a short/failed CopyBuffer    |
//|     was treated as "data available": the full path accepted a      |
//|     partial ATR/ADX copy and never read the RSI return at all, the |
//|     incremental path skipped a failed tail copy silently. Both left|
//|     g_atr_buf/g_adx_buf/g_rsi_buf zero or stale at the exact       |
//|     indexes the closed-bar decision reads, while the bar identity  |
//|     was still committed. Now: not-complete => retry (the bar is NOT|
//|     consumed), bounded so a terminal that cannot serve the history |
//|     can never block the chart, and never silent.                   |
//| AUDIT-02 [WARNING] EMA/VWAP validity: four consumers tested        |
//|     EMA != EMPTY_VALUE only, so a 0.0 EMA (unwritten tail of a     |
//|     partial copy) passed as a real value and could grant the       |
//|     EMA/VWAP confluence evidence. All eight now require > 0.0.     |
//| AUDIT-03 [WARNING] FireSetupAlert consumed its "|ALERT" dedup key  |
//|     BEFORE the publish guards, so a suppressed alert could never   |
//|     fire later. The key is now taken only when the alert is sent.  |
//| AUDIT-04 [RESOLVED v6.6.1] Version drift: QSMC_VERSION_TEXT and     |
//|     #property version now both read v6.6.1, the build that carries   |
//|     the arbitration layer and its MQL5-dialect compile fixes.         |
//| AUDIT-05 [STYLE] Dead declarations removed (4 unused entry-mark     |
//|     buffer arrays, 1 undefined prototype) and the preview plot      |
//|     arrows now use the documented hollow diamond (108/109) that     |
//|     the preview OBJECTS already use.                               |
//| Report: docs/KLJ_V6.5.2_FILE_AUDIT.md                              |
//| No threshold, gate, score weight or historical value was changed.  |
//| v6.4.1 SIGNAL VISIBILITY FIX (entries actually drawn):             |
//| V1. 4 new DRAW_ARROW plots (buffers 3-6) carry CONFIRMED (solid)   |
//|     and PREVIEW (hollow) marks for CORE + ZRE entries. Before this  |
//|     release the indicator had NO arrow plot and NO OBJ_ARROW at all. |
//| V2. Entry/SL/TP1/TP2 get per-signal trend lines + price labels keyed  |
//|     by signal bar (no name collisions), driven by ShowEntries/ShowSLTP.|
//| V3. The top-down "institutional confirmation" veto is now optional    |
//|     (InpRequireInstitutionalConfirm=false default): grade A/B/C on the   |
//|     label instead of a silent block that made BOTH directions         |
//|     unpublishable on every WAIT bar.                                  |
//| V4. Label registry cap 256 -> 512 + overflow guard, and a label that  |
//|     finds no free pixel slot now stays at its anchor instead of being  |
//|     hidden (InpHideLabelIfNoRoom=true restores the old behaviour).     |
//| V5. Chase filter: an entry too far from the zone edge is labelled      |
//|     "LATE - wait for retest" instead of vanishing.                     |
//| V6. Dedup: one mark per zone+direction until invalidated; tactical     |
//|     CONFIRMED alerts no longer re-fire on every execution bar.         |
//| V7. No repaint: the tactical path can no longer CONFIRM on a forming   |
//|     M5/M1 bar (live_cross is preview-only).                             |
//| V8. Zone Reaction Engine: BROKEN is now role-aware (support closes      |
//|     below its low, resistance closes above its high).                   |
//| Hidden signal export moved to buffers 7-18 (QSMC_Tester constants       |
//| updated).                                                               |
//| v6.5.0 REACTION SIGNAL LAYER (RXN) - the missed-SELL fix:            |
//| A1. NEW LAYER between ZRE observation and core execution authority.   |
//|     It CLASSIFIES market state into WATCH -> REACTION -> STRONG       |
//|     REACTION -> CONFIRMED -> EXECUTION READY, so a reaction at a major |
//|     level is visible and explainable on the bar it happens, BEFORE any |
//|     retest/RR/geometry exists. It places no orders and authorizes no   |
//|     entry; EXECUTION READY is mirrored from the core engine only.     |
//| A2. BUG-02 fixed: displacement is a FOLLOW-THROUGH property, searched |
//|     on the bars AFTER the rejection. On the rejection bar itself       |
//|     wick/range >= 0.50 forces body/range <= 0.50, below the 0.55 that  |
//|     AnalyzeCandleIntelligence requires, so the group could never fire. |
//| A3. BUG-04 fixed: the reaction reads the EXISTING liquidity master     |
//|     (EQH/EQL pools, BSL/SSL TAKEN children) through the existing       |
//|     sorted price index. "No pool in range" is NOT_APPLICABLE, so       |
//|     NO SWEEP no longer means NO REACTION.                             |
//| A4. BUG-05 fixed: an armed setup owns the EXECUTION lane, not          |
//|     OBSERVATION. A CONFIRMED opposite reaction can now release it      |
//|     through the existing LifecycleInvalidateActive terminal path.     |
//| A5. BUG-09/10/11 fixed: zone strength is split into intrinsic quality  |
//|     and the HTF/D1 context term; ZRE's published number is unchanged,  |
//|     but the zones it dropped or truncated for DRAWING reasons are now   |
//|     reachable for DETECTION. HTF/D1 is charged once, contextually.    |
//| A6. BUG-06/07/08/12 fixed: vetoed reactions no longer display or alert |
//|     as REACTION CONFIRMED; FLIPPED no longer erases a reaction; the    |
//|     unreachable statement after a return is gone; the ZRE signal ring   |
//|     no longer silently evicts an OPEN row.                            |
//| A7. Volatility regime (the existing g_quant.vol_class) now adapts the  |
//|     penetration budget and TIGHTENS displacement in EXTREME, so news   |
//|     continuation is not read as a reversal and a large candle is not   |
//|     read as displacement. No NFP-specific rule exists anywhere.       |
//| A8. Suppression diagnostics: every candidate that is not promoted      |
//|     states the level it reached, the evidence present and missing, and |
//|     the exact reason. A bare "NO TRADE" is no longer possible.        |
//| No existing threshold was changed; no gate was loosened; no engine was |
//| duplicated. Audit: docs/KLJ_V6.5.0_REACTION_LAYER_AUDIT.md            |
//| Report: docs/KLJ_V6.5.0_REACTION_LAYER_REPORT.md                      |
