//| P3.   Price-action feature engine: body/wick/range ratios,         |
//|      ATR-normalized body/range, close location, rejection and      |
//|      engulfing flags.                                              |
//| P4.   StructureEvent ledger with origin / confirmation /           |
//|      availability times and parent links (BOS / CHOCH / MSS).      |
//| P5.   Liquidity ledger (BSL/SSL/EQH/EQL/PDH/PDL/PWH/PWL, session,  |
//|      internal/external) with status UNTOUCHED..INVALIDATED.        |
//| P6.   Sweep engine (a wick alone is never a sweep): penetration,   |
//|      wick/body ratio, close location, reclaim, ATR depth, HTF      |
//|      context.                                                      |
//| P7.   Displacement engine reporting DisplacementStrength (0-100),  |
//|      never a probability.                                          |
//| P8.   Strict causal sequence                                       |
//|      LIQUIDITY->SWEEP->DISPLACEMENT->MSS->OB/FVG->RETEST->LTF      |
//|      CONFIRMATION->ENTRY READY with event ids.                     |
//| P9.   OB/FVG linkage to the source displacement / MSS.             |
//| P10.   Price-location vector: premium/discount/equilibrium on      |
//|      D1/H4/H1 plus ATR-normalized distances to pools and           |
//|      PDH/PDL/PWH/PWL.                                              |
//| P11.   Volatility and regime engine                                |
//|      (TREND/RANGE/EXPANSION/CONTRACTION/HIGH VOL/LOW VOL) feeding  |
//|      the historical matching.                                      |
//| P12.   Session engine, UTC internally; Algeria (UTC+1) appears in  |
//|      the panel only. A session is context and never an automatic   |
//|      signal.                                                       |
//| P13.   Recursive binary research tree: BuildMarketTree /           |
//|      AnalyzeMarketNode / SearchRecursive / DestroyMarketTree with  |
//|      maxDepth, minSegmentSize and a hard recursion cap.            |
//| P14.   Historical analogue search on a 22-dimension feature vector |
//|      with MFE/MAE/RR/time-to-target outcomes and censored samples. |
//| P15.   Conditional price paths A/B/C (id, direction, target        |
//|      liquidity, invalidation, required vs current conditions,      |
//|      analogues, MFE/MAE, RR distribution,                          |
//|      ACTIVE/WAITING/INVALIDATED/COMPLETED).                        |
//| P16.   Conditional statistics with explicit sample size, period,   |
//|      market and timeframe; rates are withheld below the minimum    |
//|      sample size and are never presented as a probability.         |
//| P17.   ConfluenceScore kept strictly separate from any rate: it is |
//|      weighted evidence (0-100) and can never authorise an entry.   |
//| P18.   Upgraded market-intelligence panel: PRICE / HTF CONTEXT /   |
//|      LOCATION / LIQUIDITY / CAUSAL SEQUENCE / MARKET REGIME /      |
//|      HISTORICAL ANALOGUES / PRICE PATHS / CURRENT STATE /          |
//|      explanation / NO-TRADE.                                       |
//| P19.   Explanation engine naming the evidence and the exact missing |
//|      condition; NO TRADE is a first-class state.                   |
//| P20.   Causal replay engine: per-bar digests are re-derived later  |
//|      from raw bars, reporting REPAINT / LOOKAHEAD / CAUSALITY PASS |
//|      or FAIL.                                                      |
//| P21.   Walk-forward view (TRAIN / VALIDATION / OUT-OF-SAMPLE) with |
//|      sample size, wins/losses, expectancy, profit factor, avg RR,  |
//|      MAE, MFE - descriptive only: no tuning, no hidden losing      |
//|      periods.                                                      |
//| P22.   Performance: closed-bar dedupe, cached per-TF series,       |
//|      incremental tree extension, throttled panel redraw.           |
//| P23.   Memory: DestroyMarketTree frees every node; allocation and  |
//|      free counters are printed at deinit; allocation is            |
//|      NULL-checked.                                                 |
//| P24.   Data-quality gate (missing/duplicate/invalid OHLC, coverage, |
//|      spread anomalies): unusable data is never a valid observation. |
//| P25.   Six explicit scenario self-tests (an incomplete sequence can |
//|      never become ENTRY READY) executed at initialization.         |
//| P26.   The layer is strictly observational: it never creates,      |
//|      mutates, invalidates or authorises a setup. Entry authority   |
//|      remains CalculateAITradeSetup / ManageSetupLifecycle.         |
//|                                                                    |
//| REVIEW FIXES v6.1.1 (research layer only; no entry-path change):    |
//| R1.   tools/verify_predictive.py still asserted the pre-refactor    |
//|      pointer tree ('new MarketTreeNode', 'delete'): the repository  |
//|      gate reported 4 FAILs. The harness now verifies the pool      |
//|      allocator (single ArrayResize in PMI_NewNode, post-order free, |
//|      allocation/free accounting) and runs the new tree model test.  |
//| R2.   PMI_TreeCausalityCheck flagged EVERY internal node of a       |
//|      healthy tree: the right-child test required                  |
//|      right.startIndex == node.endIndex+1, which no correctly built  |
//|      node can satisfy. The replay audit therefore published         |
//|      "CAUSALITY FAIL" permanently. The check now asserts the real   |
//|      invariant (children contiguous and inside the parent, node     |
//|      ends where its right child ends).                             |
//| R3.   PMI_TreeExtendRightmost extended only the deepest node: every  |
//|      right-spine ancestor kept its build-time endIndex, so ancestor |
//|      statistics excluded all bars after the last rebuild and the    |
//|      root segment no longer covered the newest bar. Each spine node |
//|      now advances its own endIndex (and the leaf counter is kept    |
//|      honest when a terminal node splits).                           |
//| R4.   PMI_ChartBarForTime scanned bar times from the newest bar     |
//|      downwards and returned the first match, so it could only ever  |
//|      return the last bar index (or -1): every historical structure  |
//|      event was stamped onto the current bar (MSS event ring, node   |
//|      event attribution). It is now the earliest bar at/after t, by  |
//|      binary search on the chronological time array.                 |
//| R5.   The structure-event dedupe window was the last 24 ledger rows |
//|      - shorter than one collection pass over 8 timeframes - so each |
//|      rebuild re-appended the whole ledger (unbounded growth, and    |
//|      per-node event loops over it). The dedupe now scans every      |
//|      retained row of that timeframe, stopping at the origin time.   |
//| R6.   Session high/low liquidity levels were stamped with the       |
//|      session's first bar instead of the bar that set the extreme,   |
//|      so bars preceding the extreme counted as touches of a level    |
//|      that did not exist yet.                                        |
//| R7.   SearchRecursive indexed query[8] without a dimension guard    |
//|      (would be "array out of range" if called with a shorter        |
//|      vector); the read is now bounded by dim / ArraySize(query).    |
//| R8.   PMI_PrepareAxisCache covered the OLDEST PMI_AXIS_MAX bars of  |
//|      the research range, so with InpPMISnapshotCap > 2200 every     |
//|      recent bar had no axis class and splits silently degraded to   |
//|      the time partition. The window now keeps the newest bars       |
//|      (identical for the defaults). PMI_FirstBarAtOrAfter delegates  |
//|      to the same verified mapping instead of re-scanning history.   |
//| R9.   Walk-forward: "PF" printed 99.90 for a fold with no losing    |
//|      sample (fabricated-looking number) and "maxDD" was always     |
//|      0.00R because the equity peak was incremented unconditionally. |
//|      PF is withheld ("n/a") and maxDD is a real drawdown now.       |
//| R10.  Data-quality: the "duplicated timestamps" branch was          |
//|      unreachable (the non-monotonic test already covered it), so    |
//|      the counter could never be reported.                           |
//| R11.  Structure-event dedupe: replace the all-ledger scan with a    |
//|      bounded 4096-key ring + open-address index. Equality remains  |
//|      timeframe/originTime/direction; evicted keys expire from the  |
//|      dedupe horizon.                                               |
//|                                                                    |
//| PHASE 59 DASHBOARD FIXES (display layer only; no decision change):  |
//| D1.   RepositionDashboard() stacked ALL five color-legend labels    |
//|      on the same x: after any CHARTEVENT_CHART_CHANGE (resize,      |
//|      scale change) the legend collapsed into an overlapping pile    |
//|      until the next full draw. It now rebuilds the exact draw       |
//|      layout (accumulated offsets from each label's OBJPROP_TEXT).   |
//| D2.   RepositionDashboard() never moved the accent strip DASH_STRIP:|
//|      after a chart resize the strip stayed at the old x, detached   |
//|      from the panel border. It now follows the panel background.    |
//| D3.   RepositionDashboard() used text offset bg_x+8 while the draw  |
//|      body uses bg_x+10: every chart-change event nudged the text    |
//|      2px sideways. Both paths now share the same +10 pad and the    |
//|      same panel-font fallback (0 -> 9).                             |
//| D4.   Stale version strings: the three dashboard titles printed     |
//|      "v6.0", the init banner "v6.0.0" and the stop banner "v5.8.0"  |
//|      while the build is v6.1.1. All now come from one macro         |
//|      QSMC_VERSION_TEXT (guard absent from this checkout).           |
//| D5.   PMI panel row cap raised 44 -> 64: in DASH_FULL the base rows |
//|      plus EXPLANATION/RESEARCH/WALK-FORWARD could reach the old cap |
//|      and silently truncate the research tail. Array, cap and stale  |
//|      label cleanup loop are kept in sync.                           |
//| D6.   COMPACT mode read g_trade_setup.reasons[0] without checking   |
//|      reason_count, so a previous setup's stale reason text could    |
//|      mislabel the current ZONE row (e.g. "BULLISH OB+FVG" with no   |
//|      setup at all). The read is now guarded by reason_count>0.       |
//| D7.   v7 file: DashRow() was unbounded while DashClearRest() cleans |
//|      only rows 0..63; rows created at index >= 64 would never be    |
//|      deleted on rebuild. DashRow now caps at the same 64.           |
//|      Evidence: tools/dash_reposition_model_test.py (A-E all PASS),  |
//|      verify_engine.py updated to the macro-based title.             |
//|                                                                    |
//| v6.1.3 CHART LAYOUT AUDIT - ITERATION 2 (display layer only; no     |
//| decision, scoring, causal or setup-lifecycle change):               |
//| L1.   Panels are no longer permanent full-size overlays. The        |
//|      Dashboard, MTF-alignment and PMI panels start COLLAPSED into   |
//|      the unified verdict badge (verdict + one-line reason + a row   |
//|      of [+] DASH / [+] MTF / [+] PMI buttons). Each panel expands   |
//|      only on CHARTEVENT_OBJECT_CLICK of its button and collapses    |
//|      again from the same button or its own title row. The idle     |
//|      badge is capped at InpPanelIdleMaxHeightPct (15%) of the chart |
//|      height (rows are dropped to fit) and its width is capped so it |
//|      never reaches the newest InpPanelReserveBars (30) visible      |
//|      candles. SafeLeftPanelWidth() now measures that boundary from  |
//|      the real bar geometry (ChartTimePriceToXY, chart shift aware)  |
//|      instead of an averaged 20-bar estimate. Collapsed panels still |
//|      run their data refresh (causal diagnostics, MTF alignment), so |
//|      the verdict never goes stale while a panel is hidden.          |
//| L2.   Label-collision resolver: every OBJ_TEXT the indicator draws   |
//|      (S/R tags, BOS/CHoCH/MSS, JUDAS, candle-battle markers, early  |
//|      break, MTF entry, provisional fractals) is registered with its |
//|      desired anchor. After each draw pass (and on every chart       |
//|      scroll/zoom) a single pass keeps an in-memory list of placed   |
//|      pixel rects and moves each new label (flip side, then step     |
//|      away in InpLabelMinGapPx increments) until it clears every     |
//|      already-placed label in the visible range. A label that cannot |
//|      be placed anywhere is hidden rather than drawn on top of text. |
//| L3.   Confluent S/R clustering tolerance widened 0.18 -> 0.5 ATR    |
//|      (InpConfluentSRMergeATR) plus a post-pass that re-merges       |
//|      clusters whose averaged centres drifted within tolerance; the  |
//|      renderer also refuses to draw two levels closer than that.     |
//|      The S/R text now lives only on the SR_TAG label (line/band     |
//|      carry it as a tooltip), so "show object descriptions" can no   |
//|      longer print the same text three times on top of itself.       |
//| L4.   "SELL 0.3 at 84418.00" root cause: this indicator never reads  |
//|      or prints lot sizes - that text is the terminal's own trade    |
//|      level label (open position / pending order, drawn by MT5 at    |
//|      the left edge of the price pane). It cannot and must not be    |
//|      deleted, so panels now compute keep-out bands from the actual  |
//|      positions/orders (+SL/TP) on this symbol and are placed clear  |
//|      of them (InpPanelsAvoidTradeLevels).                           |
//| L5.   Stale-object fixes found during the audit: (a) the MTF        |
//|      execution-entry line/label survived two early returns in       |
//|      UpdateMTFExecutionEntry() and could stay on the chart after    |
//|      its condition lapsed; (b) PrepareDynamicRedraw() deleted the    |
//|      non-existent prefixes "STR_"/"ZN_" while the objects are named |
//|      "STRUCT_"/"ZONE_", so stale BOS/CHoCH labels and zones piled   |
//|      up on top of the current ones; (c) OnInit now removes any      |
//|      QSMC_ objects left by a previous session/mode before drawing.   |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| v6.2.0 MASTER VOLUME PROFILE (observational, display only)       |
//| Closed-bar volume-at-price: daily master, and session profiles.  |
//| POC / VAH / VAL / HVN / LVN / naked POC. Tick volume by default. |
//| Buy/sell split is close-location, not bid/ask. Does not score,   |
//| gate, mutate or authorize a setup.                                |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| v6.3.0 ZONE REACTION ENGINE (ZRE) - observational, additive      |
//| 1. ZONES  : one SZREZone list from g_confluent_sr, causal OB/FVG,|
//|    active g_mvp POC/VAH/VAL/HVN, PDH/PDL/PWH/PWL, merged inside  |
//|    InpConfluentSRMergeATR. ZONE STRENGTH 0-100 (touches 20,      |
//|    sources 20, tier 10, swept 10, HTF 14, D1 6, freshness 20).   |
//| 2. STATES : IDLE / APPROACHING / TOUCHED_PREVIEW (live candle,   |
//|    unconfirmed) / REACTION_CONFIRMED / BROKEN / EXPIRED, derived |
//|    statelessly from closed bars. One alert per zone+state+bar    |
//|    (popup / push / sound, minimum zone strength).                |
//| 3. REJECTION on the CLOSED bar: touch, bounded penetration,      |
//|    reclaim close, and >= InpZREMinEvidence independent evidence  |
//|    groups. A wick alone is never a rejection; a close inside     |
//|    the zone cancels it.                                          |
//| 4. ZONE REACTION SCORE 0-100 = zone 30, rejection 25, volume 10, |
//|    HTF/D1 15, location 10, room to barrier 10. It measures the   |
//|    quality of the evidence. It is NOT a probability or win rate. |
//| 5. PATH   : entry, SL, TP1-3 (FindInstitutionalTarget, capped by |
//|    NearestOpposingBarrier), STOP ZONE at TP3, <= 3 projections,  |
//|    deleted on TP3 / SL / InpZREProjectBars timeout. RR1 gate.    |
//| 6. BEST ZONE ENTRY (score X/100) or NO TRADE + reason. SMC       |
//|    CONFLUENCE is a display tag read from the setup engine.       |
//| 7. UI     : lines in the existing dashboard only; labels go      |
//|    through DrawTextLabel (collision resolver). No new panel.     |
//| 8. LOG    : signal data and outcome data are separate; MFE/MAE,  |
//|    time to target, censored count; no frequency is shown before  |
//|    InpMinHistoricalSampleSize, and n is always shown.            |
//|    ZRE_SelfTest() at init. No orders, no trading functions, no   |
//|    change to CalculateAITradeSetup / ManageSetupLifecycle.       |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
#property copyright "Quantum SMC Intelligence Engine"
#property version   "6.69"
// PHASE 59 (dashboard fixes) D4: single source of truth for the build
// version shown on the dashboard titles and in the init/deinit journal
// banners. The titles used to hardcode "v6.0"/"v6.0.0" and the stop banner
// "v5.8.0" while the file itself was v6.1.1 - three different versions for
// one build. Use this macro everywhere a user-visible version is printed.
// v6.5.2 AUDIT: this macro was still "v6.5.0" while the file already carried
// 13 v6.5.1 and 23 v6.5.2 fixes in its body, so every dashboard title, the
// init/deinit banners and the journal named a build that did not contain the
// code that was running (audit rule: version bump). The macro, the
// #property version and the banner now use this release's value (v6.6.3).
#define QSMC_VERSION_TEXT "v6.6.9"
#property indicator_chart_window
#property indicator_buffers 19   // 0-2 lines, 3-6 entry marks (plotted), 7-18 hidden signal export (SigLog, INDICATOR_CALCULATIONS)
#property indicator_plots   7
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//| v6.6.0 SIGNAL ARBITRATION LAYER                                  |
//| A strict-OOP arbitration subsystem is pulled in here. It adds    |
//| ONE root object (CQuantumRoot) and routes every signal path      |
//| (CORE / ZRE / RXN / MTF-tactical) through the same gate chain.    |
//| Install the companion folder before compiling:                    |
//|   <data folder>/MQL5/Include/QSMC/*.mqh                           |
//| If the include cannot be resolved, set InpArbEnabled=false and    |
//| the indicator behaves exactly like v6.5.5.                        |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
#include <QSMC/QSMC_Root.mqh>
// v6.6.0 QSMC_ARB_PATCH_MARKER
#property indicator_label1  "EMA Fast"
#property indicator_type1   DRAW_LINE
#property indicator_color1  clrDodgerBlue
#property indicator_width1  1
#property indicator_label2  "EMA Slow"
#property indicator_type2   DRAW_LINE
#property indicator_color2  clrOrange
#property indicator_width2  2
#property indicator_label3  "VWAP"
#property indicator_type3   DRAW_LINE
#property indicator_color3  clrGold
#property indicator_width3  1
#property indicator_style3  STYLE_DOT
//--- v6.4.1 SIGNAL VISIBILITY: entry marks are PLOT buffers, not only objects.
//--- Confirmed = solid arrow, Preview = hollow diamond. EMPTY_VALUE = nothing.
#property indicator_label4  "Entry BUY (confirmed)"
#property indicator_type4   DRAW_ARROW
#property indicator_color4  clrLime
#property indicator_width4  2
#property indicator_label5  "Entry SELL (confirmed)"
#property indicator_type5   DRAW_ARROW
#property indicator_color5  clrTomato
#property indicator_width5  2
#property indicator_label6  "Entry BUY (preview)"
#property indicator_type6   DRAW_ARROW
#property indicator_color6  clrAqua
#property indicator_width6  1
#property indicator_label7  "Entry SELL (preview)"
#property indicator_type7   DRAW_ARROW
#property indicator_color7  clrMagenta
#property indicator_width7  1

double BufEmaFast[], BufEmaSlow[], BufVWAP[];
// v6.4.1 SIGNAL VISIBILITY: entry mark plots (see OnInit bindings 3-6).
// CONFIRMED = solid arrow, PREVIEW = hollow marker, EMPTY_VALUE = no signal.
// Declared here (next to the other plotted buffers) because UpdateMTFExecutionEntry
// writes the tactical mark from inside OnCalculate's per-tick path.
double BufEntryBuy0[], BufEntrySell0[];
double BufPrevBuy0[],  BufPrevSell0[];
// v6.5.2 AUDIT: BufEntryBuy[]/BufEntrySell[]/BufPrevBuy[]/BufPrevSell[] were
// declared here (and preceded by a comment claiming they were "plots 4-7")
// but never bound with SetIndexBuffer and never written anywhere in the file:
// dead declarations that made the real plot bindings (buffers 3-6 = Buf*0[])
// ambiguous to a reader. Removed - plots 4-7 are BufEntryBuy0/BufEntrySell0/
// BufPrevBuy0/BufPrevSell0, as bound in OnInit.
//--- Shared global indicator buffers (Rule 14 & Rule 21)
double g_atr_buf[], g_adx_buf[], g_rsi_buf[];

//====================================================================
// ENUMS
//====================================================================
enum ENUM_MIN_GRADE
{
   GRADE_D = 1,
   GRADE_C = 2,
   GRADE_B = 3,
   GRADE_A = 4,
   GRADE_APLUS = 5
};

enum ENUM_CAUSAL_EVENT_TYPE
{
   CE_LIQ_POOL=0,
   CE_LIQ_SWEEP,
   CE_DISPLACEMENT,
   CE_BOS,
   CE_CHOCH,
   CE_MSS,
   CE_ORDER_BLOCK,
   CE_FVG,
   CE_HTF_STRUCTURE,
   CE_SETUP,
   CE_TARGET,
   // v6.5.0 REACTION SIGNAL LAYER: a zone reaction becomes a first-class graph
   // node so the existing ancestry machinery (IsCausallyConnected,
   // FindNearestCausalAncestor, CausalGraphFingerprint, ValidateCausalGraphInvariants)
   // polices it instead of a parallel graph being built. Appended LAST so no
   // existing enumerator value changes. parent_primary = the swept liquidity pool
   // (or the zone's source event when no pool exists), parent_secondary = the
   // displacement event once it lands. RXN never links a CE_ZONE_REACTION into a
   // CE_SETUP ancestry: the reaction is an OBSERVATION node, not an authority node.
   CE_ZONE_REACTION
};

enum ENUM_BROKER_DST_RULE
{
   BROKER_DST_NONE=0,
   BROKER_DST_EU,
   BROKER_DST_US
};

enum ENUM_SESSION_ID
{
   SESSION_ASIA=0,
   SESSION_LONDON,
   SESSION_NEWYORK
};

// AUDIT-SB1 POWER OF 3 phase. Its own enum, appended after ENUM_SESSION_ID so
// no existing enumerator value anywhere in the file changes.
//   ACCUMULATION  the Asia session range is formed and has not been swept
//   MANIPULATION  that range was swept and the bar closed back inside it
//   DISTRIBUTION  the move AWAY from the sweep has followed through on a
//                 closed bar, by at least InpP3DistributionMinATR x ATR
// A phase is a description of what has already happened on closed bars. It is
// never an instruction, and it never authorizes anything.
enum ENUM_P3_PHASE
{
   P3_PHASE_NONE=0,        // no Asia range resolved for the applicable local day
   P3_PHASE_ACCUMULATION,
   P3_PHASE_MANIPULATION,
   P3_PHASE_DISTRIBUTION
};

// AUDIT-WY1 Wyckoff range event. Its OWN enum, added as a new type, so no
// existing enumerator value anywhere in the file can shift.
enum ENUM_WYCKOFF_EVENT
{
   WY_EVENT_NONE=0,      // no qualifying range, or no qualifying test bar
   WY_EVENT_SPRING,      // wick below the range low,  close back inside -> bullish
   WY_EVENT_UPTHRUST     // wick above the range high, close back inside -> bearish
};

// v6.0 MarketConflictEngine (master-prompt Sections 5 & 12).
// Classifies the relationship between the current chart's structural
// direction (the "LTF" from this engine's perspective) and the higher
// timeframe structural bias (g_htf_bias), so a lower-timeframe move against
// an intact higher-timeframe trend is labeled a retracement rather than
// blindly treated as a fresh signal in the opposite direction.
enum ENUM_MTF_CONFLICT_STATE
{
   MTF_NEUTRAL=0,       // HTF bias undetermined; no conflict claim possible
   MTF_ALIGNED,         // LTF direction matches HTF bias
   MTF_LTF_RETRACEMENT, // LTF direction opposes HTF bias, but HTF trend intact
   MTF_CONFLICT         // LTF MSS opposes an HTF bias independently confirmed by D1
};

//====================================================================
// INPUTS
//====================================================================
input group "====== EMA & VWAP ======"
input int InpEMAFast = 50;
input int InpEMASlow = 200;
input group "====== Oscillators ======"
input int InpATRPeriod = 14;
input int InpADXPeriod = 14;
input int InpRSIPeriod = 14;
input group "====== Structure (BOS/CHoCH/MSS) ======"
input int InpSwingFractalN = 3;
input int InpMaxStructureShown = 6;
input double InpDisplacementATR = 0.9;   // was 1.5; MSS label + leg net (see docs/SIGNAL_VISIBILITY_DIAGNOSIS.md)
input group "====== Order Blocks ======"
input int InpMaxStrongOB = 3;
input int InpOBTransparency = 88;
input double InpOBMaxHeightATR = 3.0;
//--- AUDIT-OB1 ORDER BLOCK LIFECYCLE COMPLETION. The OB engine already detects,
//--- scores, indexes, caps, draws and mitigates order blocks (DetectOrderBlocks,
//--- ScoreOrderBlock, SelectEntryOB, BuildOBPriceIndex/StrengthIndex,
//--- BinarySearchNearestOB, DrawStructureAndOB, AddBreakerBlock). These four
//--- inputs add ONLY what it was missing - an age bound - plus two opt-ins and a
//--- display vocabulary. There is no second OB engine and no parallel registry.
//--- Every one defaults to today's behaviour bit-for-bit: with all four left
//--- alone, no order block is created, sized, scored, drawn or retired differently.
//--- No version prefix is used on purpose: the release triple still reads v6.6.9
//--- while the file already carries v6.6.10/v6.6.11/v6.6.12 markers, and picking
//--- the next release number is a release decision (docs/QSMC_V6.6.10_TACTICAL_
//--- AUTHORITY.md defect 4), not something a module should pre-empt.
input bool   InpOBUseAgeExpiry       = false;  // retire an OB after InpOBMaxAgeBars closed bars (false = today: only a close through the zone retires it)
input int    InpOBMaxAgeBars         = 200;    // closed CHART bars; <=0 disables even when the switch is on
input bool   InpOBZoneBodyOnly       = false;  // zone = pure candle body instead of the default body+rejection-wick hybrid
input bool   InpOBShowLifecycleLabel = false;  // append FRESH/MITIGATED/BROKEN/EXPIRED to the OB box label (display only)
input group "====== Demand / Supply Zones ======"
input int InpZoneLookback = 150;
input int InpMaxZonesShown = 3;
input double InpZoneBaseBodyATR = 0.6;
input double InpZoneMaxHeightATR = 2.0;
input group "====== Breaker Blocks ======"
input bool InpShowBreakers = true;
input int InpMaxBreakersShown = 2;
input group "====== Fair Value Gaps ======"
input double InpFVGMinSizeATR = 0.2;     // was 0.3; more causal FVGs qualify (docs/SIGNAL_VISIBILITY_DIAGNOSIS.md)
input int InpMaxFVGShown = 3;
input bool InpMergeFVG = true;
input bool InpHideFilledFVG = true;
input group "====== Liquidity ======"
input int InpLiquidityLookback = 100;
input int InpLiquidityFractalN = 2;
input double InpLiqToleranceATR = 0.15;
input double InpLiquidityTolerancePips = 5.0;
input int InpMaxLiquidityShown = 3;
input group "====== Premium Features ======"
input bool InpShowKillZones = true;
input bool InpShowSessionHL = true;
input group "====== Sessions & Levels ======"
input bool InpShowPivots = true;
input bool InpShowCamarilla = true;
input bool InpShowPDHPDL = true;
input bool InpShowConfluentSR = true;
input int InpMaxConfluentSRLevels = 5;       // renderer clamps to 3..5
// Session hours are LOCAL market clocks in v5.6.
input int InpAsianStart = 9, InpAsianEnd = 18;      // Tokyo local session (09:00-18:00 JST = 00:00-09:00 UTC)
input int InpLondonStart = 8, InpLondonEnd = 16;   // London local session
input int InpNewYorkStart = 8, InpNewYorkEnd = 16; // New York local session
// Kill Zones are independent local-market windows; they are not derived from
// the first three session hours.
input int InpLondonKillZoneStart = 7, InpLondonKillZoneEnd = 10;   // London local
input int InpNewYorkKillZoneStart = 7, InpNewYorkKillZoneEnd = 10; // New York local
input group "====== Session Clock / DST ======"
input int InpBrokerUTCOffsetWinterMinutes = 120;
input ENUM_BROKER_DST_RULE InpBrokerDSTRule = BROKER_DST_EU;
input bool InpUseDSTSessions = true;
input group "====== Final Signal Resolver (AUDIT-RS1, one verdict everywhere) ======"
input bool   InpUseFinalResolver     = false; // ONE verdict for card STATUS, tactical
                                              // label wording and the tooltip. Off =
                                              // every surface keeps its own wording.
input int    InpResWeightBias        = 25;    // resolver weight: HTF/D1 bias
input int    InpResWeightZone        = 25;    // resolver weight: causal zone role under price
input int    InpResWeightReaction    = 30;    // resolver weight: reaction evidence
input int    InpResWeightTactical    = 20;    // resolver weight: tactical trigger cross
input int    InpResMinScore          = 60;    // weighted points a lone side needs = CONFIRMED
input group "====== Weighted Gate Scoring (AUDIT-GS1, evidence weighted, vetoes hard) ======"
input bool   InpUseWeightedGates     = false; // OFF = the existing hard-AND chain, unchanged
input int    InpWGWeightLevel        = 25;    // weight: level reached the alert minimum
input int    InpWGWeightEvidence     = 25;    // weight: evidence score reached InpWGMinEvidenceScore
input int    InpWGWeightProximity    = 20;    // weight: distance to the zone within InpAlertMaxDistanceATR
input int    InpWGWeightAlignment    = 15;    // weight: HTF + D1 signed context agrees
input int    InpWGWeightRoom         = 15;    // weight: room to the opposing zone not exhausted
input int    InpWGMinScore           = 60;    // weighted points a candidate needs to be published
input int    InpWGMinEvidenceScore   = 68;    // evidence floor for the evidence leg (mirrors the
                                              // existing 68; changes no shipped threshold)
input double InpWGMinRoomATR         = 1.0;   // room to the opposing zone, in ATR units
input group "====== Scalping Strategies (AUDIT-SC1, M1-M5, display only, advisory) ======"
input bool   InpEnableScalping           = false; // overlay switch: six scalping strategies
input bool   InpScalpShowOnDashboard     = false; // add the advisory line to the tooltip
input int    InpScalpWeightMomentum      = 20;    // SC-MOM  closed-bar displacement burst
input int    InpScalpWeightEdge          = 20;    // SC-EDGE zone-edge fade with MR stretch
input int    InpScalpWeightSilverBullet  = 15;    // SC-SB   inside a resolved SB window
input int    InpScalpWeightPowerOf3      = 15;    // SC-P3   after the Judas swing resolves
input int    InpScalpWeightWyckoff       = 15;    // SC-WY   spring / upthrust at the boundary
input int    InpScalpWeightConfluence    = 15;    // SC-CF   the Confluence Engine agrees
input int    InpScalpMinScore            = 60;    // weighted points needed to name a scalp
input double InpScalpDispATR             = 0.40;  // SC-MOM displacement, ATR (SCALPER preset)
input double InpScalpStopATR             = 0.80;  // advisory stop distance, ATR units
input double InpScalpTargetATR           = 1.20;  // advisory target distance, ATR units
input double InpScalpMinRR               = 1.20;  // refuse below this RR (SCALPER preset)
input double InpScalpMaxSpreadATR        = 0.10;  // HARD VETO: spread cost above this ATR ratio
input bool   InpScalpRequireSession      = true;  // HARD VETO: London/New York kill zones only
input group "====== Decision Journal (AUDIT-OBS1, per-bar why-no-entry, display only) ======"
input bool   InpEnableDecisionJournal  = false; // record one row per CLOSED bar
input int    InpObsJournalBars         = 60;    // rows kept in the ring buffer (10..500)
input int    InpObsTooltipBars         = 8;     // rows shown in the tooltip, newest first
input bool   InpObsLogEvents           = false; // Print only bars where something decided
input bool   InpObsShowResolver        = true;  // column: the resolver's verdict
input bool   InpObsShowGate            = true;  // column: the weighted gate's outcome
input bool   InpObsShowScalp           = true;  // column: the scalping overlay's verdict
input bool   InpObsShowPrimary         = true;  // column: what was actually published
input group "====== All Seven Modules At Once (AUDIT-UX1) ======"
input bool   InpEnableAllModules        = false;  // one switch: all seven strategy modules ON plus
                                             // their tooltip output. Does NOT enable the chart-object
                                             // opt-ins (SB entry zone, WY range box, OB label): boxes on
                                             // the chart are clutter, and clutter was the complaint.
input bool   InpRedrawTradeBoxOnNewBarOnly= false;  // stop the per-tick object churn of the trade box and
                                             // its five SL/TP levels. Their values are closed-bar state,
                                             // so nothing visible is lost; a confirmation that lands
                                             // mid-bar without a detection update waits for the next bar.
input group "====== Silver Bullet / Power of 3 (AUDIT-SB1, display only) ======"
// Every switch below defaults to OFF. With them off, nothing in this group is
// computed, drawn, logged or appended to the dashboard, and no existing value,
// threshold or label changes. Both modules are DISPLAY-ONLY: they publish a
// description of closed-bar history and never feed the arbiter, the Core
// lifecycle, the Directional Scenario Engine or any buffer.
input bool   InpEnablePowerOf3          = false;  // derive the A/M/D phase from the Asia range DetectJudasSwing already computes
input bool   InpP3ShowOnDashboard       = false;  // append the phase to the dashboard tooltip (needs InpEnablePowerOf3)
input double InpP3DistributionMinATR    = 1.00;   // closed-bar move away from the manipulation extreme, in ATR
input bool   InpEnableSilverBullet      = false;  // windowed sweep -> structure shift -> FVG -> retrace query
input bool   InpSBShowOnDashboard       = false;  // append the Silver Bullet state to the dashboard tooltip
input bool   InpSBShowEntryZone         = false;  // draw the FVG retrace zone the window resolved to
// Windows are MINUTES FROM LOCAL MIDNIGHT so they are exact to the minute and
// independent of chart timeframe. They are resolved through the SAME broker
// clock the session engine already uses (InpBrokerUTCOffsetWinterMinutes +
// InpBrokerDSTRule + InpUseDSTSessions), so no second time conversion is
// introduced and a DST change cannot desynchronise the two.
input bool   InpSBUseNYLocalTime        = true;   // true = windows are New York local; false = broker-server local
input int    InpSBWin1Start = 180, InpSBWin1End = 240;   // window 1, 03:00-04:00
input int    InpSBWin2Start = 600, InpSBWin2End = 660;   // window 2, 10:00-11:00
input int    InpSBWin3Start = 840, InpSBWin3End = 900;   // window 3, 14:00-15:00
input int    InpSBChainMaxAgeBars       = 240;    // a chain element older than this many closed bars cannot open a window setup
input group "====== Wyckoff Spring / Upthrust (AUDIT-WY1, display only) ======"
// Display only. This module never feeds the arbiter, the Core lifecycle, the
// Directional Scenario Engine, the confluence scorers, or any buffer, and it
// cannot authorize, arm or execute a trade.
//
// The RANGE is found by expanding left from the last closed bar while the
// running height stays inside InpWyckoffMaxRangeATR, so it is the actual
// consolidation rather than an arbitrary fixed window. It is deliberately NOT
// DetectDealingRange(): that finds the swing range for premium/discount and is
// meant to be large, while a Wyckoff range is meant to be tight. Different
// measurement, so nothing is duplicated.
input bool   InpEnableWyckoff           = false;  // detect Spring / Upthrust at a structural range
input bool   InpWyckoffShowOnDashboard  = false;  // append the event to the dashboard tooltip (needs InpEnableWyckoff)
input bool   InpWyckoffShowRange        = false;  // draw the range box the event was measured against
input int    InpWyckoffMinRangeBars     = 16;     // a range shorter than this is noise, not accumulation
input int    InpWyckoffMaxRangeBars     = 240;    // leftward expansion stops here
input double InpWyckoffMaxRangeATR      = 6.00;   // max range height in ATR - above this it is a trend, not a range
input int    InpWyckoffMinTouches       = 2;      // required tests of EACH boundary
input double InpWyckoffTouchTolATR      = 0.25;   // how close to a boundary still counts as touching it
input bool   InpWyckoffRequireVolume    = true;   // require the existing displacement-or-volume sweep confirmation
input int    InpWyckoffMaxAgeBars       = 96;     // an event older than this many closed bars is stale
input group "====== Pure Price Action (AUDIT-PA1, display only) ======"
// The unified pattern function ALREADY EXISTS: AnalyzeClosedCandle() returns one
// pattern label and one 0-100 strength for nine patterns, and a "Pin Bar" is its
// HAMMER / SHOOTING_STAR geometry. This module does not reimplement any of that.
// It adds the one pattern from the brief that was missing (Inside Bar, which
// lived only in PMI's g_pmi_pa.inside_bar) and, above all, it enforces the rule
// the brief asks for and the existing scorer does not: a candle pattern is
// CONFIRMATION ONLY inside a valid zone, never standalone.
input bool   InpEnablePriceAction        = false;  // unify patterns and require a zone for confirmation
input bool   InpPAShowOnDashboard        = false;  // append the price-action verdict to the dashboard tooltip
// OPT-IN, DEFAULT OFF. ContextualCandleScore() currently awards candle.score*0.45
// with NO zone requirement, then adds the zone as a BONUS (+12 zone_ok, +8 inside).
// So a candle outside every zone still contributes. Turning this on makes the zone
// a hard requirement and such a candle scores 0. While it is off - the default -
// ContextualCandleScore() is bit-identical to what it was before this change.
input bool   InpPARequireZoneContext     = false;  // make the zone a prerequisite, not a bonus
input bool   InpPAIncludeInsideBar       = true;   // add INSIDE_BAR to the unified pattern set
input int    InpPAInsideBarStrength      = 45;     // an inside bar carries no direction of its own
input double InpPAZoneToleranceATR       = 0.15;   // how close to a zone still counts as inside it
input bool   InpPAIncludePOC             = true;   // count the active volume-profile POC as a zone
input group "====== Mean Reversion / Momentum (AUDIT-MR1, display only) ======"
// THREE legs, and what each one is allowed to do. The BANDS (VWAP +/- k sigma,
// reusing the existing BufVWAP rather than adding iBands) say price is stretched.
// RSI DIVERGENCE says the stretch is exhausting, and is measured on CONFIRMED
// swings only - IsFractalHigh()/IsFractalLow(), which require InpSwingFractalN
// fully closed bars to the right, so a swing can never un-confirm itself. MACD is
// an optional momentum FILTER ONLY: it can veto a fade, and it can never add a
// direction or a point of its own. Missing evidence scores 0, never a free point.
input bool   InpEnableMeanReversion     = false;  // master switch; while off the module costs nothing
input bool   InpMRShowOnDashboard       = false;  // append the mean-reversion verdict to the dashboard tooltip
input int    InpMRStdDevPeriod          = 20;     // closed bars used for the sigma of (close - VWAP)
input double InpMRBandSigma             = 2.00;   // band width in sigma; a close beyond it is an overextension
input int    InpMRDivLookback           = 200;    // closed bars searched for the two confirmed swings
input double InpMRDivMinRSIDelta        = 2.00;   // minimum RSI gap that counts as divergence, not noise
input double InpMRRSIOverbought         = 70.0;   // RSI at or above this makes a stretched-up bar exhausted
input double InpMRRSIOversold           = 30.0;   // RSI at or below this makes a stretched-down bar exhausted
// OPTIONAL momentum filter. The iMACD handle is created ONLY when this is true,
// so with the default off nothing in OnInit changes at all. If the handle cannot
// be created the leg reports "unavailable" and scores 0 - an optional display-only
// filter must never be able to stop the indicator from loading.
input bool   InpMRUseMACD               = false;  // use MACD as a veto on fading against momentum
input int    InpMRFastEMA               = 12;     // MACD fast EMA (standard 12)
input int    InpMRSlowEMA               = 26;     // MACD slow EMA (standard 26)
input int    InpMRSignalSMA             = 9;      // MACD signal SMA (standard 9)
input double InpMRMacdDeadZoneATR       = 0.05;   // histogram must clear this fraction of ATR to count as momentum
input group "====== Confluence Engine (AUDIT-CF1, display only) ======"
input bool   InpEnableConfluence        = false;  // master switch for the ONE unified score; while off it costs nothing
input bool   InpCFShowOnDashboard       = false;  // show the confluence block in the dashboard tooltip
input int    InpCFWeightStructure       = 20;     // weight: structure (MSS/BOS/CHoCH alignment), 0-100
input int    InpCFWeightLiquidity       = 20;     // weight: liquidity (swept pool alignment), 0-100
input int    InpCFWeightZone            = 20;     // weight: zone (price inside a live OB/FVG/SR/POC), 0-100
input int    InpCFWeightSession         = 10;     // weight: session (kill zone / London / NY / Asia), 0-100
input int    InpCFWeightCandle          = 15;     // weight: candle (unified pattern strength, zone required), 0-100
input int    InpCFWeightMTF             = 15;     // weight: MTF bias (higher-timeframe closed structure), 0-100
input int    InpCFMinDisplayScore       = 60;     // minimum score to name a side; below it the engine stands aside
input bool   InpCFVetoOnConflict        = true;   // NO TRADE when a source that HAS evidence contradicts the side
input bool   InpCFRequireActiveStrategy = false;  // additionally require one strategy module (P3/SB/WY/PA/MR) to agree
input group "====== Risk Model (AUDIT-RM1, display only, advisory text) ======"
input bool   InpEnableRiskModel         = false;  // master switch for the advisory Entry/SL/TP/R:R readout
input bool   InpRMShowOnDashboard       = false;  // show the risk readout in the dashboard tooltip
input double InpRMSLBufferATR           = 0.30;   // ATR buffer beyond the zone or pool the stop sits behind
input double InpRMSLMaxATR              = 2.00;   // hard cap on stop distance in ATR; beyond it the plan is rejected
input double InpRMNoZoneSLATR           = 1.50;   // stop distance in ATR when no zone and no pool sits behind entry
input bool   InpRMUseRRFloor            = true;   // reject when TP1 R:R is below the file's hard floor InpTopDownMinRR
input bool   InpRMPreferTopDownPlan     = true;   // adopt the TopDown chain's own entry/SL/TP1 when it agrees
input int    InpRMMaxPoolScan           = 40;     // how many recent liquidity pools to scan for the stop and targets
input group "====== Premium / Discount & OTE ======"
input bool InpShowPremiumDiscount = true;
input bool InpPDLinesOnly = false;          // draw range boundaries / EQ as Fibonacci-style lines
input bool InpShowFibonacci = false;
input bool InpShowOTE = true;
input int InpSwingLookback = 120;
input int InpSwingRangeFractalN = 8;
input double InpOTEFibStart = 0.618;
input double InpOTEFibEnd = 0.79;
input group "====== v5.0 Algorithm Settings ======"
input bool InpUseDynamicProg = true;
input bool InpUseKnapsack = true;
input bool InpUseGraphTheory = true;
input group "====== QUALITY ENGINE - FLEXIBLE ======"
input bool InpRelaxedMode = true;
input bool InpAllowPartialFVG = true;
input int InpMinReliability = 80;
input ENUM_MIN_GRADE InpMinGrade = GRADE_B;
input bool InpBlockLowGrade = false;
input int InpMinEntryOBStrength = 3;
input double InpMaxOBDistATR = 8.0;
input bool InpAlertOnSetup = true;
input int InpMinConfidenceScore = 75;
input group "====== Panel Layout ======"
input bool InpASCIIBar = true;
input int InpPanelRightPad = 68;
input int InpPanelFontSize = 0;
// Legacy dashboard-size values are retained for saved-template compatibility.
// The current decision panel supports 10 rows with a full-width readable layout.
enum ENUM_DASH_MODE
  {
   DASH_MINI    = 0,   // Mini (recommended: ~6 rows)
   DASH_COMPACT = 1,   // Compact (grouped sections, no internals)
   DASH_FULL    = 2    // Full (all engineering details)
  };
enum ENUM_QSMC_DISPLAY_MODE
  {
   QSMC_MODE_MINIMAL  = 0, // primary scenario + top S/R only
   QSMC_MODE_STANDARD = 1, // compact dashboard and useful context
   QSMC_MODE_FULL     = 2  // all display families allowed, still capped at 8 dashboard rows
  };

//--- v5.8.0 Quant Engine enums -----------------------------------------
// VWAP reset anchor. DAILY reproduces the v5.7.5 default exactly
// (broker calendar-day anchor). The other anchors are computed with the
// same pure-time session math already used by the session engine; no
// local-clock reads, no look-ahead.
enum ENUM_VWAP_RESET
  {
   VWAP_RESET_DAILY   = 0,   // Daily (broker calendar day)
   VWAP_RESET_WEEKLY  = 1,   // Weekly (broker Monday 00:00)
   VWAP_RESET_LONDON  = 2,   // London session open
   VWAP_RESET_NEWYORK = 3    // New York session open
  };

// Volume source for VWAP and the volume features. Tick volume is the
// honest default for forex/CFD; real volume is only used when it is
// genuinely present in the chart data (never silently assumed).
enum ENUM_QUANT_VOL_SOURCE
  {
   QVS_TICK = 0,   // Tick volume (default, honest for FX/CFD/metals)
   QVS_REAL = 1    // Real volume (only if broker data truly contains it)
  };

// Volatility classification (Phase 4). Description only: volatility is
// never interpreted as bullish or bearish.
enum ENUM_VOL_CLASS
  {
   VOL_LOW      = 0,
   VOL_NORMAL   = 1,
   VOL_HIGH     = 2,
   VOL_EXTREME  = 3,
   VOL_UNKNOWN  = 4
  };

// Displacement quality (Phase 5).
enum ENUM_DISP_QUALITY
  {
   DISP_NONE     = 0,
   DISP_WEAK     = 1,
   DISP_MODERATE = 2,
   DISP_STRONG   = 3,
   DISP_EXTREME  = 4
  };

// Sweep quality (Phase 7).
enum ENUM_SWEEP_QUALITY
  {
   SWEEP_NONE        = 0,
   SWEEP_WEAK        = 1,
   SWEEP_VALID       = 2,
   SWEEP_HIGH_QUALITY= 3
  };

// Analytical breakeven state (Phase 33). Display only.
enum ENUM_BE_STATE
  {
   BE_NOT_READY = 0,
   BE_CANDIDATE = 1,
   BE_CONFIRMED = 2
  };

// Deterministic Core Confirmed signal lifecycle. PREVIEW is provisional and
// can never confirm or journal a setup; confirmation is always a later close.
enum ENUM_SIGNAL_STATE
  {
   STATE_WATCH                  = 0,
   STATE_ARMED                  = 1,
   STATE_PREVIEW                = 2,
   STATE_CONFIRMATION_PENDING   = 3,
   STATE_CONFIRMED              = 4,
   STATE_TARGET_1_REACHED       = 5,
   STATE_TARGET_2_REACHED       = 6,
   STATE_TARGET_3_REACHED       = 7,
   STATE_INVALIDATED            = 8,
   STATE_EXPIRED                = 9,
   STATE_COMPLETED              = 10,
   STATE_NO_TRADE               = 11
  };

//--- Phase 4 Institutional Behavior Classification
enum ENUM_INSTITUTIONAL_BEHAVIOR
  {
   IB_NONE                            = 0,
   IB_ACCUMULATION_LIKE               = 1,
   IB_DISTRIBUTION_LIKE               = 2,
   IB_STOP_RUN_SWEEP                  = 3,
   IB_FAILED_BREAKOUT                 = 4,
   IB_DISPLACEMENT                    = 5,
   IB_REACCUMULATION_CONTINUATION     = 6,
   IB_REDISTRIBUTION_CONTINUATION     = 7,
   IB_REJECTION_FROM_PREMIUM          = 8,
   IB_REJECTION_FROM_DISCOUNT         = 9
  };

//--- Phase 9 Setup Ranking Rank
enum ENUM_SETUP_RANK
  {
   RANK_PRIMARY   = 0,
   RANK_SECONDARY = 1,
   RANK_WEAK      = 2,
   RANK_NONE      = 3
  };
input ENUM_DASH_MODE InpDashMode = DASH_MINI;   // Legacy setting; current panel uses the fixed compact layout
input group "====== Clarity (1920x1080) ======"
input bool InpUltraCleanMode = true;           // clear default: outlines only; hides detailed research panels
input bool InpShowBattleAnnotations = true;
input int InpBattleAnnotationLookback = 80;
input int InpPDTransparency = 97;
input group "====== AI Dashboard ======"
input bool InpShowAIDashboard = true;
input bool InpDashboardFullWidth = false;      // v6.6.8: OFF = compact card (does not cover the chart); ON = wide strip
input int  InpDashboardMaxRows   = 6;          // Rows drawn on the card (3-10); everything else stays in the hover tooltip
input int  InpDashboardMaxWidthPx= 430;        // Pixel width cap for the compact card; the wide mode is capped at 900
input bool InpDockDashboard = true;            // Legacy positioning setting; compact Core panel is left-docked
input bool InpDashboardCollapsible = true;     // Click Core title row to show/hide the three detail rows
input bool InpShowMTFPanel = true;              // Legacy toggle; MTF is shown as Core-dashboard context
input bool InpShowTradeBox = true;
input group "====== v6.1.3 Chart Layout (panels / labels) ======"
input bool   InpPanelsStartCollapsed   = true;  // Legacy setting; Core details always start collapsed
input int    InpPanelReserveBars       = 30;    // Newest visible candles no panel may ever cover
input int    InpPanelIdleMaxHeightPct  = 15;    // Max % of chart height used by the idle (collapsed) badge
input bool   InpPanelsAvoidTradeLevels = true;  // Keep panels clear of the terminal's order/position labels
input double InpConfluentSRMergeATR    = 0.5;   // Confluent S/R levels closer than this x ATR merge into one
input bool   InpResolveLabelCollisions = true;  // Shift chart text labels so no two overlap
input int    InpLabelMinGapPx          = 15;    // Minimum vertical gap between chart text labels (pixels)
input group "====== Trade Levels (Pro) ======"
input bool InpDrawTradeLevels = true;
input bool InpSLBeyondSweep = true;
input double InpSLBufferATR = 0.2;
input group "====== ICT Depth & Filters ======"
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpHTFBiasTF = PERIOD_H4;
input bool InpUseHTFBias = true;
input int InpHTFStructureFractalN = 3;
input group "====== v6.4.0 TOP-DOWN DECISION ENGINE (D1 -> M5) ======"
input bool   InpTopDownEnabled = true;   // master switch: closed-bar top-down D1->M5 decision
input bool   InpTopDownGateCore = true;  // AND-gate Layer A: core cannot confirm while top-down disagrees
input bool   InpShowTopDownPanel = true; // show the TOP-DOWN decision panel
input bool   InpTopDownAlerts = true;    // alert on top-down BUY/SELL verdict flips (closed bars only)
input int    InpTopDownStructureBars = 120;  // closed bars per TF for structure + dealing range
input int    InpTopDownFractalN = 3;         // swing fractal right-side bars per TF
input int    InpTopDownSweepN = 5;           // M15 sweep lookback behind the liquidity extreme
input int    InpTopDownReactBars = 24;       // M30 reaction lookback (closed bars)
input double InpTopDownReactBodyATR = 0.5;   // M30 reaction body threshold (x ATR)
input int    InpTopDownSetupBars = 30;       // M15 sequence lookback (closed bars)
input int    InpTopDownExecBars = 12;        // M5 execution lookback (closed bars)
input double InpTopDownChaseATR = 1.5;       // max distance price may run from the entry edge (x M15 ATR)
input double InpTopDownMinRR = 2.0;          // hard R:R floor (policy: never below 1:2)
input int    InpTopDownMinConfluences = 3;   // minimum distinct-timeframe confluences to publish
input bool   InpTopDownRequireSession = false; // additionally require an active killzone
input int    InpTopDownProfileBars = 120;    // H1 bars for the value-area (POC/VAH/VAL) profile
input bool   InpShowPerfMeter = false;        // TOP-DOWN panel: show microsecond timings (runtime evidence)
input bool InpDetectJudas = true;
input int InpMaxSpreadPts = 60;
input bool InpIgnoreSpreadOffHours = false;
input bool InpIgnoreSpreadInBacktest = true;
input int InpMaxStructureAge = 40;
input double InpADXChopLevel = 18.0;
input double InpADXTrendLevel = 25.0;
input group "====== Multi-Timeframe ======"
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpMTF1 = PERIOD_MN1;
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpMTF2 = PERIOD_W1;
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpMTF3 = PERIOD_D1;
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpMTF4 = PERIOD_H4;
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpMTF5 = PERIOD_H1;
input group "====== Zone Colors ======"
input color InpColorOB = clrFireBrick;
input color InpColorOB_Bear = clrCrimson;
input color InpColorFVG = clrMediumOrchid;
input color InpColorDemand = clrSeaGreen;
input color InpColorSupply = clrDodgerBlue;
input color InpColorBreaker = clrGold;
input color InpColorPremium = clrIndianRed;
input color InpColorDiscount = clrForestGreen;
input color InpColorEQ = clrSilver;
input color InpColorFib = clrDarkGray;
input color InpColorOTE = clrAqua;
input group "====== DEBUGGING ======"
input bool InpShowDebugAlerts = false;
input bool InpLogSignalDetails = true;
input group "====== SIGNAL GATE AUDIT (why is there no signal?) ======"
input bool InpShowGateAudit = true;        // dashboard: per-gate survival + top blocker
input int  InpGateAuditLogEveryBars = 0;   // log the audit every N closed bars (0 = off)
input group "====== REAL-TIME MODE ======"
input bool InpRealTimeZones = true;
input bool InpUpdateEveryTick = true;
input bool InpRealTimeFractal = true; // draws provisional markers only; never feeds decisions
input group "====== PREVIEW LATENCY (NON-AUTHORITATIVE) ======"
input int InpMinRightConfirmBars = 1; // preview only; confirmed fractals always use N right bars
input bool InpShowEarlyBreakPreview = true; // non-authoritative live break preview
input double InpEarlyBreakBufferPoints = 0.0; // extra points required beyond structure price
input bool InpShowEarlyBreakTrigger = true; // show the same authoritative structure level before the break

input group "====== SETUP -> RETEST -> CONFIRMED (NEW v5.2.0) ======"
input bool InpUseRetestLifecycle = true;
input double InpInvalidateBufferATR = 0.3;
input bool InpAlertOnSetupReady = false;
input bool InpShowEntryPreview = true; // live entry preview on retest; non-authoritative
input bool InpAlertOnEntryPreview = true; // legacy template field; live PREVIEW is chart-only (closed-bar alerts only)
input bool InpInvalidateOnOppositeMSS = true; // closed opposite MSS cancels active setup and releases opposite scan
input group "====== MTF EXECUTION ENTRY (TACTICAL, NON-AUTHORITATIVE) ======"
input bool InpUseMTFExecutionEntry = true;
input bool InpAutoExecutionTF = true;
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES InpExecutionTF = PERIOD_M5;
input double InpMTFEntryMaxDistanceATR = 1.0;
input bool InpAlertOnMTFExecutionEntry = true;
input bool InpShowMTFExecutionEntry = true;
input group "====== v6.4.1 SIGNAL VISIBILITY / ENTRIES ======"
input bool   InpShowEntries             = true;   // draw CONFIRMED entries as arrows + label on the chart
input bool   InpShowEntryPreviewMarks   = true;   // draw PREVIEW (live/unconfirmed) entries as hollow markers
input bool   InpShowSLTP                = true;   // draw Entry / SL / TP1 / TP2 lines + price labels
input double InpMinStrength             = 0.0;    // 0-100 minimum quality score required to DRAW a mark (0 = draw all)
input bool   InpRequireInstitutionalConfirm = false;  // true: top-down/institutional grade becomes a HARD veto (legacy behaviour)
input bool   InpShowTacticalEntries     = true;   // draw the MTF (tactical) entry: arrow + label, not only an HLINE
input bool   InpChaseFilter             = true;   // late-entry filter: distance from close to the entry edge in ATR
input double InpChaseMaxATR             = 1.50;   // beyond this x ATR the entry is stale -> "LATE - wait for retest"
input double InpEntryLabelATR           = 0.45;   // arrow/label offset from the bar, in ATR
input bool   InpAlertOnConfirmed        = true;   // Alert() popup on CONFIRMED (once per signal)
input bool   InpAlertPushOnConfirmed    = false;  // SendNotification() push on CONFIRMED
input bool   InpAlertOnSignalBar        = true;   // tactical alert/label/arrow anchor on the signal bar (exec bar = false)
input bool   InpShowZREEntryMarks       = true;   // draw the selected primary ZRE/RXN reaction mark
//--- v6.4.1 label stack: entries must survive a crowded chart.
input bool   InpHideLabelIfNoRoom       = false;  // true: hide a text label when no free pixel slot exists (v6.1.3 behaviour)
//--- v6.4.2 AUDIT switches (Phase 2 proof logging + Phase 3 filters).
input bool   InpDebugLog                = false;  // Phase-2 proof log: every direction decision + every veto reason
input bool   InpVetoContrarySignalDirection = false; // true: a zone whose ROLE contradicts the candidate direction is refused (default: logged only)
input int    InpSignalDedupCooldownBars = 3;      // minimum bars between two marks of the same zone+direction key
input bool   InpProximityFilter         = true;   // refuse an entry that sits right under strong resistance (BUY) / right over strong support (SELL)
input double InpProximityMaxATR         = 0.35;   // ...within this many ATR of the opposing edge
input int    InpLabelFontSize           = 0;      // chart label font (0 = per-element default, 7 recommended with Clean)
input int    InpMaxChartObjects         = 0;      // hard cap on QSMC_* chart objects per pass (0 = 1200, 900 with Clean)
input int    InpMaxZonesPerSide         = 5;      // demand / supply boxes drawn per side (Clean forces 2)
input bool   InpDeclutterMode           = true;   // Clean preset: fewer zones, small labels, capped objects

input group "====== v5.4.0 Performance & Stability ======"
input bool   InpUseIncrementalDetection = true;
input int    InpMaxStructuresKeep      = 30;
input int    InpMaxLiquidityKeep       = 40;
input int    InpMaxFVGKeep             = 25;
input int    InpMaxZonesKeep           = 20;
input int    InpRetestTimeoutBars      = 40;    // was 25; retest window (docs/SIGNAL_VISIBILITY_DIAGNOSIS.md)
input double InpRetestMaxDistanceATR   = 4.0;   // was 2.5; retest reach (docs/SIGNAL_VISIBILITY_DIAGNOSIS.md)
input bool   InpSmartObjectManagement  = true;
input bool   InpLogLifecycleTransitions = false;

input group "====== v5.6.6 RUNTIME / CAUSAL VALIDATION ======"
input bool InpRuntimeNoLookaheadAudit = true;
input int  InpRuntimeAuditBars = 500;

input group "====== v5.6.6 ADVANCED CAUSAL SWEEP ENGINE ======"
input bool   InpUseAdvancedSweepEngine      = true;
input double InpSweepEntryMinScore          = 75.0;
input int    InpSweepEntryMaxBarsAfterSweep = 3;
input double InpSweepEntryMinRR             = 1.50;
input bool   InpUseMergeSortRanking         = true;
input bool   InpUseMemoizedDP               = true;
input bool   InpUseFibonacciDP              = true;
input bool   InpUseCausalGraphOptimizer      = true;
input bool   InpUseDijkstraPathSearch         = true;
input bool   InpUseBellmanFordValidation      = true;
input bool   InpUseBeamSearch                 = true;
input int    InpBeamWidth                     = 5;
input int    InpGraphMaxPathHops              = 8;
input double InpGraphTemporalPenaltyATR       = 0.04;
input double InpGraphConflictPenalty          = 2.50;
input double InpGraphCausalReward             = 3.00;
input bool   InpRejectGraphNegativeCycle      = true;
input bool   InpRequireGraphAgreement         = false;
input bool   InpUseCausalDPOptimizer           = true;

input group "====== v5.6.9 CAUSAL DIAGNOSTICS ======"
input int    InpWatchMinQuality            = 75;

input group "====== v5.6.8 ALGORITHMIC CONFLUENCE ENGINE ======"
input bool   InpUseEvidenceIndependence      = true;
input bool   InpUseRegimeAdaptiveScoring     = true;
input bool   InpUseContextualCandleScoring   = true;
input double InpRegimeExpansionBonus         = 1.05;
input double InpRegimeTrendBonus             = 1.03;
input double InpRegimeRangePenalty           = 0.92;
input double InpRegimeCompressionPenalty     = 0.88;

input group "====== v6.0 PRIME LEVEL ENGINE (diagnostic-only) ======"
// PrimeLevelEngine: prime-number-derived price levels as an OPTIONAL
// statistical/confluence feature. Per design, this must never gate or
// authorize entry -- it only ever contributes a small, capped bonus to the
// diagnostic score, exactly like the existing EMA/VWAP confluence bonus.
input bool   InpUsePrimeLevels           = true;
input int    InpPrimeLevelCount          = 25;    // how many prime-derived levels to generate per side
input double InpPrimeLevelToleranceATR   = 0.15;  // proximity tolerance, ATR-normalized
input double InpPrimeScoreMaxBonus       = 2.0;   // hard cap on final_score contribution (points)
input bool   InpUseRelationshipMatrix    = true;
input double InpRelationshipScoreMaxBonus = 2.0;  // hard cap on final_score contribution (points)
input double InpMTFConflictPenalty       = 4.0;   // hard cap on final_score penalty for MTF_CONFLICT (points)

input group "====== v5.6.5 UNIVERSAL INSTRUMENT ADAPTER ======"
input bool InpUniversalInstrumentMode = true;
input bool InpUseExchangeTickSize      = true;
input bool InpUseBrokerStopsGeometry   = true;

enum ENUM_QSMC_GATE_PROFILE
  {
   QSMC_GATE_STRICT    = 0,   // STRICT: every threshold is the input as entered (default)
   QSMC_GATE_PRACTICAL = 1    // PRACTICAL: the five numeric entry thresholds are relaxed, and logged at init
  };

input group "====== v6.6.12 GATE PROFILE (explicit, logged, default STRICT) ======"
// STRICT: every threshold is exactly the input you see (the shipping behaviour).
// PRACTICAL: the five numeric entry thresholds below are relaxed to the values
// printed at init, one line per change ("old -> new"). It is never silent, it
// never touches the causal chain, the blacklist, the journal or the EA's risk
// logic, and it never overrides a stricter value you typed yourself. It makes
// MORE trades possible; it does not make them better.
input ENUM_QSMC_GATE_PROFILE InpGateProfile = QSMC_GATE_STRICT; // STRICT = inputs as entered | PRACTICAL = documented relaxations

input group "====== v5.6.3 Causal Institutional Sequence ======"
input bool   InpInstitutionalSequence       = true;
input int    InpSweepToStructureMaxBars     = 8;
input bool   InpRequireMSSAfterSweep         = false; // was true; MSS-only anchor was the top blocker (docs/SIGNAL_VISIBILITY_DIAGNOSIS.md)
input bool   InpAllowFVGEntryZone            = true;
input int    InpOrderZonePreSweepBars        = 1;
input bool   InpBlockEquilibriumEntries      = true;
input double InpEquilibriumBufferATR         = 0.15;
input bool   InpUseEMAVWAPConfluence         = true;
input double InpMaxStopATR                   = 4.0;   // was 3.0; also reused by ZRE (docs/SIGNAL_VISIBILITY_DIAGNOSIS.md)
input double InpMinRR1                       = 1.5;   // v6.4.2: audit required 1.5 (was 2.0) for TP1
input int    InpBlacklistExpiryBars          = 200;

input group "====== v5.6.3 Causal Event Graph ======"
input int    InpMaxCausalEventsKeep          = 160;
input int    InpAnchorSearchBars             = 60;
input double InpCausalDisplacementBodyATR    = 0.35;  // was 0.50; impulse/FVG body gate (docs/SIGNAL_VISIBILITY_DIAGNOSIS.md)
input bool   InpRequireCausalFVGBody          = true;
input bool   InpPreferMSSAnchor               = true;
input bool   InpEnableCausalInvariantChecks   = true;
input int    InpReplayAuditEveryBars          = 50;    // 0 disables incremental-vs-full audit

input group "====== v5.8.0 QUANT ENGINE (diagnostic-only) ======"
// The quantitative layer measures and classifies observable market data.
// It NEVER authorizes, gates or blocks an entry: the causal architecture
// of v5.6-v5.7 remains the only authority. All features are closed-bar,
// ATR-normalized and deterministic (identical on replay/refresh/restart).
input bool                 InpUseQuantEngine        = true;   // Master switch for the quant layer
input int                  InpATRBaselineBars       = 50;     // ATR baseline SMA window
input int                  InpATRPercentileBars     = 200;    // ATR percentile ranking window
input double               InpATRLowRatio           = 0.75;   // LOW volatility ratio  (ATR/baseline)
input double               InpATRHighRatio          = 1.30;   // HIGH volatility ratio
input double               InpATRExtremeRatio       = 2.00;   // EXTREME volatility ratio
input int                  InpVolumeAvgBars         = 20;     // Volume baseline window
input double               InpVolumeSpikeRatio      = 1.60;   // Volume spike threshold (x baseline)
input ENUM_QUANT_VOL_SOURCE InpQuantVolumeSource   = QVS_TICK; // Volume source (VWAP + features)
input ENUM_VWAP_RESET      InpVWAPReset             = VWAP_RESET_DAILY; // VWAP reset anchor (default = v5.7.5 behavior)
input ENUM_TIMEFRAMES      InpQuantEMATF            = PERIOD_CURRENT;   // EMA Slow TF for quant context (>chart TF = MTF, closed candles only)
input int                  InpEMASlopeBars          = 5;      // EMA slope lookback (closed bars)
input double               InpEMASlopeFlatATR       = 0.02;   // |slope|/ATR below this = FLAT
input double               InpLateEntryMaxATR       = 1.50;   // Late-entry risk threshold (ATR from zone)

input group "====== v5.8.0 ENTRY QUALITY ENGINE ======"
// Transparent soft-score model (Phase 21). The hard gates remain the
// existing causal/retest/confirmation architecture and are mirrored,
// never duplicated. Soft scores only RANK valid candidates.
input bool   InpShowEntryQualityPanel = true;   // Show STRUCTURAL/CONTEXT/EXECUTION/GEOMETRY rows
input double InpQualityHighThreshold  = 75.0;   // final blend >= this  -> HIGH_QUALITY
input double InpQualityAPlusThreshold = 88.0;   // final blend >= this  -> A_PLUS

input group "====== v5.8.0 ANALYTICAL SCALING (NO ORDERS, EVER) ======"
// Purely analytical/visual scaling plan. No OrderSend, no position
// modification: this is an INDICATOR.
input bool   InpUseAnalyticalScaling = true;   // Master switch for scale-in/out analysis
input double InpScale0AllocationPct  = 40.0;   // Initial allocation %
input double InpScale1AllocationPct  = 30.0;   // Scale 1 allocation % (requires NEW evidence)
input double InpScale2AllocationPct  = 30.0;   // Scale 2 allocation % (requires NEW evidence)
input double InpTP1ExitPct           = 25.0;   // TP1 exit % of position
input double InpTP2ExitPct           = 30.0;   // TP2 exit % of position
input double InpTP3ExitPct           = 45.0;   // TP3 exit % of position
input bool   InpShowScaleLevels      = true;   // Draw analytical scale trigger levels
input bool   InpUseBreakevenAnalysis = true;   // Breakeven analysis (display only)
input bool   InpAlertOnQuantEvents   = true;   // Alerts: TP reached / scale ready / BE / invalidation

input group "====== v5.8.0 REFERENCE RISK (theoretical, analytical) ======"
input double InpRiskRefVolume        = 0.10;   // Reference volume for theoretical risk (units)

input group "====== QUANTUM SMC INTELLIGENCE ENGINE (v6.0.0) ======"
input bool   InpUseCandleIntelligence       = true;  // Enable 15-point candle confirmation engine
input bool   InpUseInstitutionalBehavior    = true;  // Enable Institutional Behavior sequence analyzer
input bool   InpUseHistoricalAnalysis       = true;  // Track closed-bar setup outcomes & statistics
input int    InpMinHistoricalSampleSize     = 30;    // Minimum sample size for statistical validity

enum ENUM_MVP_MODE
{
   MVP_MODE_MASTER  = 0, // Master daily composite
   MVP_MODE_SESSION = 1, // Asia / London / New York
   MVP_MODE_BOTH    = 2, // Sessions AND daily master
   MVP_MODE_VISIBLE = 3, // Visible range
   MVP_MODE_FIXED   = 4, // Fixed bar count
   MVP_MODE_WEEKLY  = 5  // Weekly master
};

enum ENUM_MVP_ANCHOR
{
   MVP_ANCHOR_BROKER  = 0, // Broker day (00:00 server)
   MVP_ANCHOR_LONDON  = 1, // London session open
   MVP_ANCHOR_NEWYORK = 2  // New York session open
};

enum ENUM_MVP_DISTRIB
{
   MVP_DIST_TRIANGLE = 0, // Triangle at typical price (H+L+C)/3
   MVP_DIST_UNIFORM  = 1  // Uniform across the bar range
};

input group "====== v6.2.0 MASTER VOLUME PROFILE (observational) ======"
// Closed-bar volume-at-price. Never authorizes, gates or scores an entry.
// Tick volume is the honest default on FX/CFD. The buy/sell split is the
// close location inside each bar, not exchange bid/ask delta.
input bool                  InpUseMasterVolumeProfile = true;  // Master Volume Profile on/off
input ENUM_MVP_MODE         InpMVPMode                = MVP_MODE_BOTH; // Profile mode
input ENUM_MVP_ANCHOR       InpMVPDayAnchor           = MVP_ANCHOR_BROKER; // Master day boundary
input ENUM_QUANT_VOL_SOURCE InpMVPVolumeSource        = QVS_TICK; // Volume source
input ENUM_MVP_DISTRIB      InpMVPDistribution        = MVP_DIST_TRIANGLE; // Bar volume distribution
input double                InpMVPValueAreaPct        = 70.0;  // Value area percent (50-90)
input double                InpMVPRowATR              = 0.10;  // Row height as a fraction of ATR
input int                   InpMVPRowTicks            = 0;     // Fixed row in ticks (0 = ATR auto)
input int                   InpMVPWidthPct            = 14;    // Histogram width, percent of visible bars
input int                   InpMVPDayLookback         = 2;     // Trading days of master context
input int                   InpMVPSessionLookback     = 1;     // Sessions kept per region
input int                   InpMVPWeekLookback        = 4;     // Weeks of weekly context
input int                   InpMVPFixedBars           = 120;   // Bars in fixed-range mode
input int                   InpMVPMinBars             = 3;     // Minimum closed bars to publish a profile
input bool                  InpMVPShowHistogram       = true;  // Draw the volume histogram
input bool                  InpMVPShowSplit           = true;  // Buy/sell close-location split
input bool                  InpMVPShowValueArea       = true;  // Shade the active value area
input bool                  InpMVPShowHistory         = true;  // Prior POC / VAH / VAL lines
input bool                  InpMVPShowHistoryHistogram= false; // Also draw prior histograms
input bool                  InpMVPShowNakedPOC        = true;  // Untouched POC rays
input bool                  InpMVPShowNodes           = true;  // HVN / LVN ticks on the active profile
input bool                  InpMVPShowLegend          = true;  // Top-right readout
input double                InpMVPHVNFraction         = 0.60;  // HVN >= this fraction of POC volume
input double                InpMVPLVNFraction         = 0.35;  // LVN <= this fraction of median row
input bool                  InpMVPRunSelfTest         = true;  // Run the numeric self-test at init

enum ENUM_ZRE_ENTRY_MODE
{
   ZRE_ENTRY_CLOSE     = 0,   // close of the rejection bar
   ZRE_ENTRY_ZONE_EDGE = 1    // near edge of the zone
};

input group "====== v6.3.0 ZONE REACTION ENGINE ======"
// Observational. Never creates, mutates, invalidates or authorizes a setup;
// entry authority stays with CalculateAITradeSetup / ManageSetupLifecycle.
// Every confirmed ZRE fact is read on the closed bar (rates_total-2) only.
// The 0-100 numbers are evidence-quality scores, not a win rate.
input bool   InpUseZRE                 = true;   // Zone Reaction Engine on/off
input int    InpZREMaxZones            = 6;      // Keep at most this many zones (1-12)
input int    InpZREMinZoneScore        = 60;     // Minimum ZONE STRENGTH to keep a zone (0-100)
input double InpZREZonePadATR          = 0.10;   // Half-height given to single-price levels, x ATR
input double InpZREMaxZoneATR          = 1.50;   // Max source-band height; close same-side confluence may envelope two valid bands
input int    InpZREFreshBars           = 96;     // Raw default; M1/M5 presets apply while unchanged
input bool   InpZRERunSelfTest         = true;   // Run ZRE_SelfTest() at init
input bool   InpZREDebugLog            = false;  // Print the zone list on every rebuild
// ---- Stage 2: zone states and arrival alerts (closed-bar facts; live = PREVIEW)
input double InpZREApproachATR         = 0.75;   // APPROACHING when the close is within this x ATR of the zone
input double InpZREBreakATR            = 0.30;   // BROKEN when a close is beyond the zone by more than this x ATR
input int    InpZREExpireBars          = 600;    // Zone older than this many bars is EXPIRED (age known only)
input bool   InpZREAlertPopup          = true;   // legacy ZRE popup channel; routed through the shared dispatcher
input bool   InpZREAlertPush           = false;  // legacy ZRE push channel; distance/cooldown filtered
input bool   InpZREAlertSound          = false;  // legacy ZRE sound channel; distance/cooldown filtered
input int    InpZREAlertMinStrength    = 70;     // Alert only for zones with ZONE STRENGTH >= this
input bool   InpZREAlertApproaching    = false;  // Also alert on APPROACHING (noisy)
input bool   InpZREAlertBroken         = false;  // Also alert on a closed-bar broken zone (off by default for clarity)
// ---- Stage 3: rejection on the CLOSED bar (a wick alone is never a rejection)
input double InpZREMaxPenetrationATR   = 0.35;   // Max wick penetration through the far zone edge, x ATR
input double InpZREMinWick             = 0.50;   // Rejection wick >= this fraction of the bar range
input bool   InpZREInsideReclaim       = false;  // false: close must reclaim the near zone edge; true: the midpoint suffices
input int    InpZREMinEvidence         = 2;      // Independent evidence groups required (wick/engulf/sweep/volume/displacement)
input double InpZREVolSupportRatio     = 1.10;   // Volume ratio counted as supporting evidence
// ---- Stage 4-5: ZONE REACTION SCORE and projected path
input int    InpZREMinScore            = 65;     // Minimum ZONE REACTION SCORE (0-100, evidence quality) for a signal
input ENUM_ZRE_ENTRY_MODE InpZREEntryMode = ZRE_ENTRY_CLOSE; // Entry = rejection close or zone edge
input int    InpZREProjectBars         = 16;     // Projection lines/arrows end after this many bars, then are deleted
input double InpZREStopZoneATR         = 0.40;   // STOP ZONE height at TP3, x ATR
input bool   InpZREShowPath            = true;   // Draw the projected path of a confirmed reaction
input bool   InpZREShowPreview         = true;   // Draw the live PREVIEW (unconfirmed) label
// ---- Stage 6: strongest-entry selection
input double InpZREConflictGap         = 8.0;    // BUY vs SELL closer than this many score points = NO TRADE
input int    InpZREFreshEntryBars      = 3;      // A signal is a selectable entry for this many bars
input int    InpZREWeakZoneScore       = 75;     // Zone strength below this is weak against a clear HTF bias

input group "====== v6.5.0 REACTION SIGNAL LAYER (RXN) ======"
// Sits BETWEEN raw ZRE observation and final execution authority. It classifies
// market state; it NEVER places, sizes, confirms or authorizes a trade.
//   ZONE -> LIQUIDITY -> REJECTION -> DISPLACEMENT -> STRUCTURE -> [RXN] -> CORE
// Every value below is closed-bar and availability-gated. The 0-100 numbers are
// EVIDENCE QUALITY. They are not a win rate and not a forecast: this system has
// never been statistically calibrated and nothing here claims otherwise.
// No existing default above is changed by this layer (audit section 23.1).
input bool   InpUseRXN                    = true;  // Reaction Signal Layer on/off (false = exact v6.4.2 behaviour)
input int    InpRXNTrackBars              = 24;    // Closed bars a reaction track is recomputed over (same window as TopDown_React30)
input int    InpRXNConfirmWindowBars      = 12;    // Displacement/structure must land within this many bars AFTER the rejection
input int    InpRXNAcceptBars             = 2;     // Consecutive closes beyond the far edge = MAINTAINED breakout (CASE A), not a rejection
input int    InpRXNMinZoneIntrinsic       = 60;    // Intrinsic zone quality needed to recover a level ZRE's min-score filter dropped
input int    InpRXNMaxZoneExtra           = 6;     // Recovered/tail zones RXN may evaluate beyond InpZREMaxZones (detection, not drawing)
// ---- level thresholds on RXN REACTION SCORE (evidence quality, 0-100) ----
input int    InpRXNMinReactionScore       = 45;    // LEVEL 1 WATCH -> LEVEL 2 REACTION ("the market reacted")
input int    InpRXNMinStrongScore         = 58;    // LEVEL 2 -> LEVEL 3 STRONG REACTION (requires displacement)
input int    InpRXNMinConfirmedScore      = 68;    // LEVEL 3 -> LEVEL 4 CONFIRMED (requires displacement AND structure)
input int    InpRXNPromoteScore           = 72;    // A CONFIRMED opposite reaction may release an UNCONFIRMED armed setup at/above this
// ---- v6.5.4 directional-conflict guard (the bullish-into-resistance fix) ----
input bool   InpRXNOppositionFilter       = true;  // Opposing-zone room / conflict guard for CONFIRMED (false = v6.5.3 behaviour)
input double InpRXNMinRoomATR             = 1.0;   // ATR of room to the nearest opposing zone a CONFIRMED reaction needs (a closed breakout through it exempts)
input int    InpRXNCountertrendMargin     = 8;     // Extra REACTION SCORE a CONFIRMED needs when BOTH HTF and D1 oppose it (countertrend != forbidden, just dearer)
// ---- volatility regime adaptation (reuses g_quant.vol_class; no new classifier) ----
input double InpRXNPenetrationVolMult     = 2.0;   // EXTREME volatility only: multiplier on InpZREMaxPenetrationATR (a news sweep is physically deeper)
input double InpRXNDispBodyRatioExtreme   = 0.70;  // EXTREME volatility only: body/range needed for displacement (raw range is noise there)
// ---- ownership bridge (audit BUG-05) ----
input bool   InpRXNPromoteOpposite        = true;  // A CONFIRMED opposite reaction may release an ARMED/PREVIEW setup (false = observe-only coexistence)
// ---- visibility / diagnostics ----
input bool   InpRXNShowReaction           = true;  // Full mode: detailed RXN label; primary mark is shared
input bool   InpRXNShowSuppression        = true;  // Show WHY a candidate was not promoted (never a bare "NO TRADE")
input bool   InpRXNAlerts                 = true;  // RXN alert master; minimum level is InpRXNAlertMinLevel (default CONFIRMED)
input bool   InpRXNDebug                  = false; // Print the [REACTION DEBUG] block for every candidate
input bool   InpRXNRunSelfTest            = true;  // Run RXN_SelfTest() at init
input group "====== v6.5.5 Primary Scenario / Alert Policy ======"
input int    InpRXNAlertMinLevel              = 4;    // Minimum RXN alert level: 2=REACTION, 3=STRONG, 4=CONFIRMED, 5=EXECUTION READY
input double InpAlertMaxDistanceATR            = 2.0;  // No popup/push for a zone farther than this x ATR from the closed price
input int    InpAlertCooldownBars              = 5;    // Cooldown in closed bars per (zone,direction,level)
input bool   InpUseTimeframePresets            = true; // Apply M1/M5/M15+ presets when legacy inputs remain at their defaults
input ENUM_QSMC_DISPLAY_MODE InpDisplayMode    = QSMC_MODE_FULL; // Full decision card; display-only
input double InpVisualMaxDistanceATR           = 10.0; // Hide chart zones/labels beyond this x ATR; calculations are unaffected
input bool   InpPrimaryAlertPopup               = true; // Master popup enable for the unified dispatcher
input bool   InpPrimaryAlertPush                = false; // Push for selected primary scenario only
input bool   InpPrimaryAlertSound               = false; // Sound for selected primary scenario only
input bool   InpAlertDispatcherLog              = false; // Tester/replay journal for selected and suppressed candidates

input group "====== v6.5.0 DIRECTIONAL SCENARIO ENGINE (DSE) ======"
// Planning is deliberately separate from entry authority.  The engine ranks a
// conditional BUY support plan and SELL resistance plan from the existing ZRE/RXN
// registry, but only the pre-existing Core lifecycle may mark EXECUTION READY.
input bool   InpUseDirectionalScenarioEngine = true;  // closed-bar conditional BUY/SELL plan; never authorizes an entry
input bool   InpShowScenarioPlans            = true;  // draw conditional zones/invalidation labels (no entry arrows)

#define PFX "QSMC_"
#define MAX_CAUSAL_CHILDREN 8

//--- bit masking
#define BIT_MSS           (1<<0)
#define BIT_BOS           (1<<1)
#define BIT_CHOCH         (1<<2)
#define BIT_STRONG_OB     (1<<3)
#define BIT_LIQUIDITY     (1<<4)
#define BIT_FVG           (1<<5)
#define BIT_OTE           (1<<6)
#define BIT_HTF_BIAS      (1<<7)
#define BIT_KILLZONE      (1<<8)
#define BIT_DEMAND_ZONE   (1<<9)
#define BIT_JUDAS         (1<<10)
#define MAX_GRAPH_LINKS   16
#define MAX_CAUSAL_HOPS   6

//+------------------------------------------------------------------+
//|                                                                  |
//|  v6.1.0  PREDICTIVE MARKET INTELLIGENCE (PMI) ENGINE             |
//|                                                                  |
//|  CAUSAL MULTI-TIMEFRAME MARKET INTELLIGENCE & PRICE-PATH         |
//|  RESEARCH LAYER.                                                  |
//|                                                                  |
//|  CONTRACT (see docs/PREDICTIVE_ENGINE_AUDIT.md, section 7):       |
//|   - READ-ONLY with respect to the entry authority. The only       |
//|     function that can influence what the user reads as "entry     |
//|     ready" is PMI_EntryGate(), and it can only TIGHTEN           |
//|     (authoritative_ready AND pmi_chain_complete AND data_ok).    |
//|   - Every function is a pure function of the canonical           |
//|     chronological arrays plus an explicit as_of bar bound.       |
//|     No price data from any bar > as_of is ever read.             |
//|   - Every derived outcome has a measurement horizon and a        |
//|     censoring flag; censored samples are counted and excluded,   |
//|     never silently included in a hit rate.                       |
//|   - No weighted score is ever called a probability. Observed     |
//|     frequencies are labelled ANALOGUE HIT RATE with sample size, |
//|     period, symbol and timeframe disclosed.                      |
//|   - No trading functions. Indicator only.                        |
//|                                                                  |
//+------------------------------------------------------------------+

//====================================================================
// v6.1.0 PMI — CONSTANTS
//====================================================================
#define PMI_TF_COUNT            8      // W1 D1 H4 H1 M30 M15 M5 M1
#define PMI_FV_DIM              22     // market-state feature-vector dimension
#define PMI_MAX_PATHS           3      // A / B / C conditional price paths
#define PMI_MAX_COND_STATS      8      // conditional statistics slots
#define PMI_MAX_MISSING         8      // missing-condition slots
#define PMI_MAX_TREE_RECURSION  24     // hard safety cap (independent of InpPMIMaxTreeDepth)
#define PMI_NODE_NONE           -1     // "null" node index in the g_pmi_nodes[] pool
#define PMI_TREE_AXES           8      // feature partitioning axes
//--- Causal sequence stages (Phase 10). stageIndex in MarketState uses these.
#define PMI_STAGE_NONE          0
#define PMI_STAGE_LIQUIDITY     1
#define PMI_STAGE_SWEEP         2
#define PMI_STAGE_DISPLACEMENT  3
#define PMI_STAGE_STRUCTURE     4
#define PMI_STAGE_MSS           PMI_STAGE_STRUCTURE  // legacy alias
#define PMI_STAGE_ZONE          5
#define PMI_STAGE_RETEST        6
#define PMI_STAGE_LTF           7
#define PMI_STAGE_ENTRY         8   // complete chain: entry-ready at chain level

#define PMI_DIGEST_RING         64     // per-closed-bar published digests kept for replay audit
#define PMI_MAX_LEVELS_AUDIT    40     // levels captured per digest for the replay audit
#define PMI_MAX_EVENT_LOG       200    // in-memory structured event log ring

//--- structure event types (Phase 6)
#define PMI_STRUCT_NONE         0
#define PMI_STRUCT_BOS          1
#define PMI_STRUCT_CHOCH        2
#define PMI_STRUCT_MSS          3

//--- liquidity status (Phase 7)
enum ENUM_PMI_LIQ_STATUS
{
   PMI_LIQ_UNTOUCHED   = 0,
   PMI_LIQ_APPROACHED  = 1,
   PMI_LIQ_SWEPT       = 2,
   PMI_LIQ_CONSUMED    = 3,
   PMI_LIQ_INVALIDATED = 4
};

//--- market regime (Phase 13)
enum ENUM_PMI_REGIME
{
   PMI_REGIME_UNKNOWN     = 0,
   PMI_REGIME_TREND_UP    = 1,
   PMI_REGIME_TREND_DOWN  = 2,
   PMI_REGIME_RANGE       = 3,
   PMI_REGIME_EXPANSION   = 4,
   PMI_REGIME_CONTRACTION = 5,
   PMI_REGIME_CHOP        = 6
};

//--- volatility regime (Phase 13, reuses the v5.8.0 classification vocabulary)
enum ENUM_PMI_VOLREGIME
{
   PMI_VOL_LOW     = 0,
   PMI_VOL_NORMAL  = 1,
   PMI_VOL_HIGH    = 2,
   PMI_VOL_EXTREME = 3
};

//--- sessions (Phase 14). Internally UTC (no local clock, no DST guessing
//--- beyond the broker offset already modelled by the existing engine).
enum ENUM_PMI_SESSION
{
   PMI_SESS_OFF     = 0,
   PMI_SESS_ASIA    = 1,
   PMI_SESS_LONDON  = 2,
   PMI_SESS_OVERLAP = 3,   // London / New York overlap
   PMI_SESS_NEWYORK = 4
};

//--- v6.5.1 SESSION AUDIT (F-04): the PMI session windows, stated once as
//--- named UTC hour bounds instead of as magic numbers inside an if-chain.
//--- These are the bounds the classifier ACTUALLY implements. The previous
//--- comment block claimed ASIA 00:00-09:00 and NEW YORK 12:00-21:00, but the
//--- branch order returned LONDON for 07:00-09:00 and OVERLAP for 12:00-16:00,
//--- so Asia really ended at 07:00 and New York really started at 16:00. The
//--- last branch (`h>=16 && h<21 -> NEWYORK`) was unreachable dead code.
//--- NOTE: these are FIXED reference market clocks in UTC. They are deliberately
//--- NOT the same model as the user-configurable killzones (InpAsianStart,
//--- InpLondonKillZoneStart, InpNewYorkKillZoneStart) that drive IsInSession();
//--- the divergence is documented in docs/KLJ_V6.5.1_FORENSIC_AUDIT.md.
#define PMI_UTC_ASIA_START     0
#define PMI_UTC_ASIA_END       7
#define PMI_UTC_LONDON_START   7
#define PMI_UTC_LONDON_END     12
#define PMI_UTC_OVERLAP_START  12
#define PMI_UTC_OVERLAP_END    16
#define PMI_UTC_NY_START       16
#define PMI_UTC_NY_END         21

//--- conditional price-path status (Phase 18)
enum ENUM_PMI_PATH_STATUS
{
   PMI_PATH_WAITING     = 0,
   PMI_PATH_ACTIVE      = 1,
   PMI_PATH_INVALIDATED = 2,
   PMI_PATH_COMPLETED   = 3
};

//--- no-trade codes (Phase 23)
enum ENUM_PMI_NO_TRADE
{
   PMI_NT_NONE                    = 0,
   PMI_NT_INSUFFICIENT_HISTORY    = 1,
   PMI_NT_DATA_QUALITY            = 2,
   PMI_NT_HTF_CONFLICT            = 3,
   PMI_NT_NO_LIQUIDITY            = 4,
   PMI_NT_SWEEP_WITHOUT_DISPLACE  = 5,
   PMI_NT_DISPLACE_WITHOUT_MSS    = 6,
   PMI_NT_MSS_WITHOUT_ZONE        = 7,
   PMI_NT_ZONE_INVALIDATED        = 8,
   PMI_NT_RETEST_MISSING          = 9,
   PMI_NT_LTF_CONFIRM_MISSING     = 10,
   PMI_NT_POOR_RR                 = 11,
   PMI_NT_INSUFFICIENT_SAMPLE     = 12,
   PMI_NT_CONFLICTING_PATHS       = 13,
   PMI_NT_CAUSAL_ORDER_BROKEN     = 14
};

//--- tree partitioning axes (Phase 16)
enum ENUM_PMI_TREE_AXIS
{
   PMI_AXIS_CONTEXT_DIR  = 0,   // HTF direction at segment start
   PMI_AXIS_PREMIUM_DISC = 1,   // D1 premium/discount at segment start
   PMI_AXIS_VOLATILITY   = 2,   // ATR ratio at segment start
   PMI_AXIS_SWEEP_DIR    = 3,   // last sweep direction before segment start
   PMI_AXIS_DISPLACEMENT = 4,   // displacement strength at segment start
   PMI_AXIS_MSS          = 5,   // MSS state at segment start
   PMI_AXIS_SESSION      = 6,   // session at segment start
   PMI_AXIS_STRUCTURE    = 7,   // chart structure direction at segment start
   PMI_AXIS_TIME         = 8    // fallback: index midpoint (always valid)
};

//====================================================================
// v6.1.0 PMI — INPUTS (new group; nothing existing is renamed or changed)
//====================================================================
input group "====== v6.1.0 PREDICTIVE MARKET INTELLIGENCE (research layer) ======"
// The PMI layer is an observation/research layer. It never authorizes a
// trade by itself: PMI_EntryGate() can only narrow the existing
// authoritative decision, never widen it.
input bool   InpUsePredictiveEngine     = true;   // Master switch for the PMI layer
input bool   InpShowPredictivePanel     = true;   // Draw the market-intelligence panel
input bool   InpDockPMIPanel              = true;   // Dock at lower-left, outside the newest candles
input bool   InpPMIPanelCollapsible       = true;
input int    InpPMIPanelX               = 8;      // Panel X distance (pixels)
input int    InpPMIPanelY               = 420;    // Panel Y distance (pixels)
input int    InpPMIPanelRefreshTicks    = 3;      // panel refresh (ticks) between closed bars
input int    InpPMIFractalN             = 3;      // Swing fractal N for PMI structure events
input int    InpPMIMTFWindow            = 200;    // Closed HTF bars analysed per timeframe
input int    InpPMIStructureDedupeWindow = 4096;  // Recent structure-event keys retained for duplicate checks (128..65536)
input int    InpPMILiquidityToleranceATR100 = 15; // level "approached" tolerance (ATR/100; 15 = 0.15 ATR)
input int    InpPMISweepDepthMinATR100  = 8;      // min sweep penetration, ATR/100 (8 = 0.08 ATR)
input int    InpPMISweepToMSSBars       = 12;     // sweep -> MSS causal lookback (bars)
input int    InpPMIOutcomeHorizonBars   = 60;     // analogue outcome measurement horizon (bars)
input int    InpPMIRiskATR100           = 100;    // reference risk = ATR * value/100 (100 = 1.0 ATR)
input int    InpPMITargetR100           = 200;    // analogue "target reached" threshold in R (200 = 2.0R)
input int    InpPMIKNearest             = 40;     // nearest historical analogues used for statistics
input int    InpPMIMinSamples           = 30;     // minimum sample size before a rate is published
input int    InpPMISnapshotCap          = 1500;   // retained feature-vector snapshots (ring)
input int    InpPMIMaxTreeDepth         = 6;      // recursive research tree maximum depth
input int    InpPMIMinTreeSegment       = 24;     // recursive research tree minimum segment (bars)
input bool   InpPMIIncrementalTree      = true;   // update the tree incrementally (never per tick)
input int    InpPMITreeRebuildEveryBars = 20;     // periodic full tree rebuild (bars); 0 = never
input bool   InpPMILogCSV               = false;  // write structured CSV research log
input bool   InpPMILogEvents            = false;  // print structured event log lines
input bool   InpPMIRunReplayAudit       = true;   // run the candle-by-candle replay audit
input int    InpPMIReplayAuditEveryBars = 25;     // replay audit cadence (bars)
input int    InpPMIReplayAuditBars      = 300;    // bars re-derived per replay audit
input bool   InpPMIRunSelfTestOnInit    = true;   // run the scenario self-test (Tests 1-4) at init
input bool   InpPMIRunWalkForward       = true;   // build the walk-forward (descriptive) report
input int    InpPMIWalkForwardFolds     = 3;      // TRAIN / VALIDATION / OOS folds (descriptive only)

//====================================================================
// SIGNAL OUTCOME LOG (Phase 1 measurement) - inputs
// Appended after every existing input so positional iCustom() callers
// keep their parameter order. Measurement only: nothing here gates,
// creates, mutates or authorizes a setup.
//====================================================================
enum ENUM_SIGLOG_ENTRY
{
   SIGLOG_ENTRY_PUBLISHED    = 0,   // limit at the published entry (filled only when a later bar trades through it)
   SIGLOG_ENTRY_SIGNAL_CLOSE = 1    // market fill at the close of the signal bar
};

input group "====== SIGNAL OUTCOME LOG (measurement only) ======"
// Outcomes are measured on bars AFTER the signal bar only. The CSV holds
// observed results of a logged sample; it is not a forecast.
input bool              InpSigLogCSV           = false;  // Write the per-signal outcome CSV (off = no file I/O)
input bool              InpSigLogCore          = true;   // CSV: log Layer A confirmed setups (source CORE)
input bool              InpSigLogZRE           = true;   // CSV: log Zone Reaction Engine signals (source ZRE)
input bool              InpSigLogZREShadow     = true;   // CSV: also log ZRE reactions rejected ONLY by the score gate (status SHADOW)
input ENUM_SIGLOG_ENTRY InpSigLogEntryRef      = SIGLOG_ENTRY_PUBLISHED; // Entry model used to measure R
input int               InpSigLogHorizonBars   = 60;     // Measurement window in bars (same default as the PMI horizon); then TIMEOUT at the close
input bool              InpSigLogCommonFolder  = true;   // Write to Terminal\Common\Files (false = MQL5\Files)
input string            InpSigLogFilePrefix    = "QSMC_signals"; // File name = prefix_SYMBOL_TF.csv
input bool              InpExportSignalBuffers = true;   // Fill hidden calculation buffers 3-14 (read by QSMC_Tester.mq5; nothing is drawn)
input bool              InpSigLogRunSelfTest   = true;   // Run SigLog_SelfTest() at init (diagnostic print only)
input bool              InpMTEERunSelfTest     = true;   // Run deterministic synthetic MTEE tests at init

input group "====== v6.5.2 MTF SNIPER ZONE ENGINE (7-TF Confluence) ======"
input bool              InpUseSniperZoneEngine = true;   // Enable MTF_SniperZone_Engine (W1->M5 7-TF confluence)
input bool              InpShowSniperZones     = true;   // Render Active Sniper Zones (top 3 Support + top 3 Resistance)
input double            InpSniperMinStrength   = 0.50;   // Phase 3.4d: Minimum Sniper Zone strength gate (0.0-1.0)
input double            InpSniperMinADX_H1     = 20.0;   // Phase 3.4c: Minimum H1 ADX(14) trending market gate
input bool              InpSniperSessionFilter = true;   // Golden Rule 5: London/NY timing filter (Asia requires >= 0.90)
input bool              InpSniperNewsFilter    = true;   // Golden Rule 6: +-30 min high-impact news blackout
input bool              InpSniperUseTrailing   = true;   // Phase 5.4: Trail SL behind M15 swings (0.5x ATR) after TP2
input double            InpSniperMaxRiskPct    = 1.50;   // Golden Rule 7: Advisory equity risk % per trade (1.0-2.0%)
input bool              InpSniperRunSelfTest   = true;   // Run MTF_SniperZone_SelfTest() at OnInit()

//====================================================================
// v6.5.2 MTF_SniperZone_Engine — CONSTANTS
//====================================================================
#define SNIPER_TF_COUNT           7
#define SNIPER_BARS_LOAD          200
#define SNIPER_MAX_RAW_ZONES      256
#define SNIPER_MAX_CLUSTERS       128
#define SNIPER_ACTIVE_PER_SIDE    3
#define SNIPER_ACTIVE_MAX         6

// Phase 1.2 Zone Type Enumeration Constants
#define SNIPER_TYPE_OB            1
#define SNIPER_TYPE_FVG           2
#define SNIPER_TYPE_LIQUIDITY     3
#define SNIPER_TYPE_SWING         4
#define SNIPER_TYPE_FIB           5
#define SNIPER_TYPE_VWAP          6

// Phase 2 Zone Strength Outer Weights (sum = 1.00)
#define SNIPER_W_TF               0.30
#define SNIPER_W_TYPE             0.25
#define SNIPER_W_FRESH            0.20
#define SNIPER_W_TOUCH            0.15
#define SNIPER_W_VOL              0.10

// Phase 3 Confluence Clustering & Validation Gates
#define SNIPER_MERGE_ATR_MULT     0.50
#define SNIPER_CONFLUENCE_BONUS   1.20
#define SNIPER_MIN_STRENGTH_GATE  0.50
#define SNIPER_MIN_H1_ADX         20.0

// Phase 4 Closed-Bar Entry Triggers
#define SNIPER_IDEAL_MIN_CONDS    3
#define SNIPER_IDEAL_MIN_STR      0.70
#define SNIPER_ACCEPT_MIN_CONDS   2
#define SNIPER_ACCEPT_MIN_STR     0.85
#define SNIPER_DISP_ATR_MULT      1.50
#define SNIPER_VOL_CONFIRM_MULT   1.20
#define SNIPER_ASIA_MIN_STR       0.90

// Phase 5 Trade Management Constants
#define SNIPER_SL_BUFFER_ATR      0.30
#define SNIPER_SL_HARD_MAX_H1_ATR 2.00
#define SNIPER_BE_DISP_ATR        2.00
#define SNIPER_TRAIL_M15_ATR      0.50
#define SNIPER_TP1_CLOSE_PCT      50.0
#define SNIPER_TP2_CLOSE_PCT      30.0
#define SNIPER_TP3_CLOSE_PCT      20.0

// Phase 6 8th Scoring Pillar Weight (25% of total, existing 7 scaled by 0.75)
#define SNIPER_PILLAR_WEIGHT      0.25
#define SNIPER_EXISTING_SCALE     0.75

//====================================================================
// v6.1.0 PMI — CONFIGURATION (validated copy of the inputs)
//====================================================================//====================================================================
// GLOBALS
//====================================================================
datetime g_last_bar_time = 0;
int g_oncalc_seq=0;              // bumped once per OnCalculate call
int g_mtf_align_cache_seq=-1;    // MTFAlignmentPercent() per-tick cache key
int g_mtf_align_cache_value=0;   // MTFAlignmentPercent() per-tick cache value
int h_ema_fast, h_ema_slow, h_atr, h_adx, h_rsi;
int h_ema_mtf[5];
int h_sniper_atr[SNIPER_TF_COUNT];
int h_sniper_rsi[SNIPER_TF_COUNT];
int h_sniper_adx_h1 = INVALID_HANDLE;
int g_signal_mask = 0;
double g_atr = 0.0;
double g_adx = 0.0;
long g_spread = 0;
int g_htf_bias = 0;
string g_htf_structure_state = "NEUTRAL";
string g_d1_structure_state  = "NEUTRAL";
//--- v6.4.0 top-down decision state (closed bars of D1..M5 only)
struct STopDownState
{
   bool  computed;
   bool  logged;
   int   dir;              // +1 BUY, -1 SELL, 0 WAIT
   string blocker;         // first failing step of the chain
   string reasons[16];
   int   reason_count;
   int   confluences;
   bool  tf_ok[6];
   string tf_state[6];
   double tf_eq[6];
   bool  profile_ok;
   double poc, vah, val;
   double entry, sl, tp1;
   double rr;
   string tp_src;
   datetime fp[6];
   datetime fp_next[6];       // exact next-bar open used to prove each closed leg's availability
   datetime fp_chart;
   int  last_alert_dir;
   // v6.5.2 PUBLISHED STRUCTURAL TUPLE. The chain's own logic is unchanged; these
   // are facts it already derived internally (the M15 sequence's swept price, the
   // causal OB/FVG zone it produced, and the per-leg ATRs) that used to be locals
   // of TopDown_Evaluate and therefore unreachable. Exposing them read-only is
   // what lets a downstream planner reconcile ITS zone with the chain's zone
   // instead of re-deriving (and possibly contradicting) it. A consumer may only
   // read a leg whose tf_ok[] entry is true.
   double m15_sweep;           // swept liquidity price of the M15 sequence
   double m15_zone_lo;         // causal OB/FVG zone produced by that sequence
   double m15_zone_hi;
   int    m15_sweep_bar;       // read-only source index in the closed M15 snapshot
   int    m15_displacement_bar;
   datetime m15_sweep_time;
   datetime m15_displacement_time;
   datetime m15_structure_time;
   datetime m15_structure_availability; // next M15 open after the existing break bar
   string m15_detail;          // "sweep ... -> OB/FVG ..." text, already formatted
   double m15_atr;             // M15 ATR the chase/stop geometry used
   double m30_atr;             // M30 ATR the reaction body test used
   double m5_atr;              // M5 ATR of the execution window
};
STopDownState g_td;
long g_perf_td_us=0;    // TOP-DOWN engine: EMA of evaluation time (microseconds)
long g_perf_calc_us=0;  // OnCalculate body: EMA of tick processing time (microseconds)
int g_judas = 0, g_judas_bar = 0;
//--- AUDIT-SB1 POWER OF 3. DetectJudasSwing() ALREADY computes the Asia session
//--- range and ALREADY detects a sweep of it with a close back inside - that is
//--- the Accumulation and the Manipulation leg. It simply threw the range away
//--- when it returned, because nothing needed it until now. These four retain
//--- what it computed, so the phase can be named WITHOUT a second, parallel
//--- session engine and without recomputing one bar of it.
double   g_asia_range_high=0.0;      // published by DetectJudasSwing, not recomputed
double   g_asia_range_low=0.0;
int      g_asia_range_day_key=-1;    // DateKey() of the applicable Tokyo-local day
bool     g_asia_range_valid=false;
ENUM_P3_PHASE g_p3_phase=P3_PHASE_NONE;
int      g_p3_dir=0;                 // +1 distribution up, -1 down, 0 not resolved
string   g_p3_reason="";
int      g_p3_score=0;               // 0-100 rule-based confluence count, NOT a probability
string   g_p3_invalidation="";
//--- AUDIT-SB1 SILVER BULLET. A time-windowed QUERY over the causal graph that
//--- already exists (CE_LIQ_SWEEP -> CE_BOS/CE_CHOCH/CE_MSS -> CE_FVG, linked by
//--- parent_primary/parent_secondary and walked by FindNearestCausalAncestor).
//--- It adds no detection of its own: every element it names was already
//--- published on a closed bar by an existing engine.
bool     g_sb_active=false;          // a window resolved a complete chain
int      g_sb_window=-1;             // 0..2 = which window is open, -1 = none
int      g_sb_dir=0;                 // +1 long, -1 short, 0 unresolved
int      g_sb_fvg=-1;                // index into g_causal_events of the CE_FVG element
double   g_sb_entry_high=0.0;
double   g_sb_entry_low=0.0;
string   g_sb_reason="";
int      g_sb_score=0;               // 0-100 rule-based confluence count, NOT a probability
string   g_sb_invalidation="";

//--- AUDIT-WY1 WYCKOFF SPRING / UPTHRUST (display only). The range geometry is
//--- new because nothing in the file measured a TIGHT consolidation before; the
//--- sweep confirmation is NOT new - it reuses SweepHasDisplacementOrVolume(),
//--- which already tests displacement or relative volume on existing data, so no
//--- new volume source is introduced. Reconciled against g_judas rather than
//--- allowed to contradict it: see WY_Update().
double   g_wy_range_high=0.0;
double   g_wy_range_low=0.0;
int      g_wy_range_start=-1;        // first bar of the range window
int      g_wy_range_end=-1;          // last bar of the range window (closed-1)
bool     g_wy_range_valid=false;
int      g_wy_touches_high=0;
int      g_wy_touches_low=0;
int      g_wy_event=WY_EVENT_NONE;
int      g_wy_dir=0;                 // +1 spring, -1 upthrust, 0 unresolved
int      g_wy_bar=-1;                // the closed bar the event fired on
double   g_wy_extreme=0.0;           // the wick that pierced the boundary
bool     g_wy_active=false;
bool     g_wy_volume_ok=false;
bool     g_wy_conflict=false;        // disagrees with the Judas verdict on the same bar
int      g_wy_score=0;               // 0-100 rule-based confluence count, NOT a probability
string   g_wy_reason="";
string   g_wy_invalidation="";

//--- AUDIT-PA1 PURE PRICE ACTION (display only). One pattern, one strength, and
//--- a verdict that is empty unless price is inside a valid zone. The zone scan
//--- reads the arrays the existing detectors already publish (g_order_blocks,
//--- g_fvgs, g_zones, g_mvp) and honours their own state vocabulary, so no second
//--- zone system and no second opinion about whether a zone is still alive.
string   g_pa_pattern="NONE";        // unified label from the existing 9 + INSIDE_BAR
int      g_pa_strength=0;            // 0-100
int      g_pa_pattern_dir=0;         // direction the pattern itself carries (0 = none)
bool     g_pa_inside_bar=false;
bool     g_pa_in_zone=false;
string   g_pa_zone_name="";          // OB / FVG / SR / POC
double   g_pa_zone_top=0.0;
double   g_pa_zone_bottom=0.0;
int      g_pa_zone_dir=0;
int      g_pa_dir=0;                 // resolved direction, 0 when there is no zone
bool     g_pa_confirms=false;
